{"data":[{"slug":"test-engineer-70162","company_name":"Think Cell","title":"Test Engineer (f/m/d)","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;thinkcell provides &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.notion.so/%7b%7b%20site:locale%20%7d%7d/product&quot;&gt;graphics software&lt;/a&gt; that performs most of the painstaking work of creating data-driven slides for professional Excel and PowerPoint users. The testing department makes sure that new features are technically sound and work reliably for all user groups, from new users to seasoned financial professionals.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Test Engineer at thinkcell, you&#39;ll help improve a product that over 1,000,000 professionals around the world rely on every day.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Testing and verifying new features is an important part of the job, as our product continues to evolve. Since think-cell is seamlessly integrated into Microsoft PowerPoint and Excel, we must pay close attention to its compatibility with supported Microsoft Office versions, operating systems, and their respective updates.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;There is a certain level of complexity to our product and consequently to the testing process. Problem-solving skills are important as well as keeping an overview between verifying fixes, creating test cases, and ensuring our users receive only top quality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feature Testing: Ensure new thinkcell features work properly and verify their logical consistency and usability.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Release Testing: Conduct final quality checks before each think-cell version release.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Error Reproduction and Reporting: Create detailed error reproductions and document them clearly. Provide precise information to help resolve issues and record all error-related details in the internal system.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Verification: Verify that developer fixes successfully resolve reported issues.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Knowledge Base Management: Maintain and expand the internal Knowledge Base with documentation of new product functionality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;You will be great for this position if you have&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;High level of self-motivation and independent work structuring.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosity and critical thinking.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willingness to learn and adapt to new technologies.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluency in written and spoken English.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;(Plus) Experience with Microsoft Office, particularly PowerPoint and Excel.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Our Values&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As part of our team, you will embody and help shape the following principles that define us:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Forward Thinking: We embrace change and challenge the status quo.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ownership: We take pride in our work and learn from our mistakes.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Customer First: We prioritize delivering lasting value.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unified Team: We foster collaboration, respect, and integrity.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strive for Excellence: We set ambitious goals and pursue quality.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;Why is thinkcell the right place for you?&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We empower over 1.3 million users across 35,000 companies, including top consulting firms and major global enterprises. With offices in Berlin, Munich, Denver, Boston, London, Tokyo, and Dubai, we’re a diverse team of over 220 people, committed to innovation and excellence.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;thinkcell is more than a job – it&#39;s a chance to be part of an innovative, inclusive team that values collaboration and growth. We encourage applicants from all backgrounds to apply. Together, we can shape the future of productivity software.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span data-contrast=&quot;auto&quot;&gt;We can’t wait to see what you’ll bring to the team!&lt;span data-ccp-props=&quot;{}&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/think-cell/test-engineer-70162","tags":["Development"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1793062519},{"slug":"senior-software-engineer-munich-365741","company_name":"Auterion","title":"Senior Software Engineer","description":"&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a hands-on Autonomous Drone Software Engineer to join a swarming programme. As an engineer on a lean, high-impact team, you will have the opportunity to drive development of new features, have a say in architecture and design decisions and have real impact across all the team’s projects.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You will not be siloed; this role spans the entire autonomy lifecycle, from developing autonomy capabilities to investigating real-world flight-test data.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The ideal candidate is someone who’s a self-starter, can work independently, can work with ambiguity, can take decisions on their own and not be afraid to drive and push towards getting the project across the finish line.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership and drive the development of new features across the autonomy stack and partner integrations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate closely with hardware engineers, product managers, and external partners to define system requirements and translate them into robust software architecture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design and implement robust distributed state machines, leader election protocols, and fault-tolerant architectures.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deliver clean, readable and maintainable code while confidently managing complex concurrency and contention scenarios&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Develop and run rigorous tests utilizing SITL/HITL simulation environments to validate code prior to physical deployment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Actively participate in code reviews, architectural discussions, and technical documentation to elevate the team&#39;s engineering standards&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act decisively during flight-test investigations, applying strong engineering judgment to physical failure modes and release safety&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;3+ years of professional engineering experience in robotics, embedded systems, or distributed systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deep proficiency in modern C++, with practical experience designing, reasoning about, and debugging highly concurrent systems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embedded systems experience working close to hardware on real-time or safety-critical platforms (e.g., avionics, automotive, robotics).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong architectural understanding of distributed systems, with the ability to deliberately evaluate and select consensus designs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with robust release management, versioned artifacts, and pinned dependencies.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4, MAVLink, and related drone software ecosystems is a plus&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship required&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/auterion/senior-software-engineer-munich-365741","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Munich","created_at":1793062518},{"slug":"forward-deployed-engineer-munich-444941","company_name":"Auterion","title":"Forward Deployed Engineer","description":"&lt;p&gt;As a Forward Deployed Engineer at Auterion, you will play a pivotal role in the successful development, integration and deployment of Auterion-powered drone systems.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you will collaborate closely with the production, hardware engineering, and firmware/software teams, as well as operations, ensuring that every platform transitions smoothly from an airframe concept into a fully validated flying robot ready for deployment. You will serve as the primary technical interface for partners, work closely with them to understand their technical requirements, configure and adapt existing solutions, contribute to core software development, and ensure successful implementation.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role is ideal for an engineer who enjoys combining hands-on technical work with customer collaboration and system-level problem solving, bridging the gap between hardware, firmware, and real-world flight performance.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities and Duties&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Operate in a highly hands-on environment with evolving system requirements, rapidly iterating across hardware and software integration challenges.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Manage software releases and perform firmware flashing and configuration using PX4 or adjacent autopilot ecosystems, including sensor calibration, ESC tuning, and system bring-up.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide deep avionics and airframe expertise, including autopilot tuning, sensor and payload integration, power systems and airworthiness considerations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work independently to troubleshoot integration and flight-readiness issues while collaborating cross-functionally with hardware engineering, firmware/software teams, operations, and QC engineering to escalate complex challenges when required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary technical authority in customer engagements, translating mission requirements into concrete system architectures and demonstrable solutions built on AuterionOS and Skynode.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Participate in flight testing activities to validate platform stability, safety, and mission performance, resolving technical issues often directly in the field during customer trials and demonstrations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to technical documentation and continuous improvement of engineering processes.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Feed customer and market requirements back into product and engineering teams to influence the roadmap of the Auterion stack.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualifications and Skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Degree in Software, Electrical, Mechanical, Aerospace or Robotics Engineering, or a related field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working proficiency in C/C++ and Python: you can read, debug and patch existing code and write small tools and scripts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfortable in Linux environments, including the command line, logs, Docker and basic networking (IP, TCP/UDP)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on hardware-software integration: system bring-up, wiring and connectors, and embedded interfaces (UART, CAN, I2C, SPI) at a practical level&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Structured troubleshooting: you can isolate whether a problem is software, hardware, configuration or RF, often under time pressure in the field&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong communicator: you can explain technical issues clearly to customers and operators, and report findings back to engineering in a way they can act on&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Willing to travel and work on-site with customers, including at test ranges and in field environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;EU citizenship (required for security clearance and customer requirements)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with PX4 or ArduPilot, MAVLink, QGroundControl or mission planning tools&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;UAV flight testing and validation in operational environments&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with datalinks and radio systems&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Previous customer-facing or field engineering role, especially with defense or government customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;German language skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexible working hours&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Stock Options&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Generous holiday allowance&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pension plan&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Extended social security package&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Enhanced maternity &amp;amp; paternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Wellpass membership&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Auterion&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are building the leading software platform for AI-powered autonomous systems for enterprise and government customers. Our team is supporting the most important missions and solving the most challenging problems.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Auterion, we bring together the sharpest minds who love to solve the hardest problems. Join a vibrant team built on innovation, openness, and excellence, where you’ll be empowered to develop ideas, collaborate across all levels, and make an impact that matters.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/auterion/forward-deployed-engineer-munich-444941","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Munich","created_at":1793062518},{"slug":"remote-technical-product-manager-132288","company_name":"Swarmaero","title":"Technical Product Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em">Swarm Aero is redefining air power, building the largest swarming UAV and the most versatile swarming aircraft network in the world. The company is moving quickly to launch the first aircraft designed specifically for swarming, as well as the Command &amp; Control software to mobilize swarms of thousands of heterogeneous autonomous assets and empower human operators to achieve superhuman results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The team has created and exited multiple startups, negotiated defense deals worth billions of dollars, and designed and built 30+ novel aircraft, with aerospace experience from Scaled Composites, Airbus, Archer Aviation, Blue Origin, and Boom Supersonic.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mission</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn operational needs, customer feedback, and product direction into clear product specifications—and then drive those capabilities through decisions, design, development, and validation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will work directly with the Head of Product on Legion and become a core contributor to both defining the product and running the process around it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Own</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create clear, detailed product specifications for new features and capabilities.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take customer needs, operator feedback, technical constraints, and product direction and turn them into actionable product requirements.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own bounded features from early definition through design, development, feedback, and validation.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work directly with Product Design to translate specifications into detailed workflows and Figma designs.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review designs and implementations against product intent and requirements.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Facilitate product discussions with government customers, third-party contractors, operators, engineers, and internal stakeholders.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare agendas and clearly identify topics requiring feedback, decisions, or alignment.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Capture decisions, unresolved issues, customer feedback, and action items.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Incorporate meeting outcomes directly into product specifications and related artifacts.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain feature status, decision history, feedback registers, and key product commitments.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify ambiguity, conflicting requirements, and missing decisions before they slow the team down.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track important product and contractual deliverables.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help prepare product reviews, demonstrations, and customer discussions.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create enough structure to keep the organization aligned without introducing unnecessary process.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What Great Looks Like</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are given a problem such as:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">“Operators need a better way to understand and respond to vehicle health issues during degraded communications.”</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You meet with the relevant operators, engineers, customers, and stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand the underlying problem.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You separate customer requests from actual product requirements.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You identify edge cases and unresolved decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You write a product specification that clearly explains the intended behavior, workflows, system states, requirements, and open questions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You work with Product Design to turn that specification into a strong interface.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You incorporate feedback, resolve ambiguity, and keep the feature moving until the capability works as intended.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Head of Product provides direction and reviews the most important decisions—but does not need to personally produce every artifact or manage every follow-up.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Early Expectations</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Within the first few weeks, you should begin contributing directly to product specifications.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Initially, you may draft sections of specifications or own smaller, well-bounded capabilities with guidance from the Head of Product.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As your understanding of Legion, its operators, and the technical architecture grows, you will rapidly take ownership of larger features.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are not looking for someone who spends six months observing before contributing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The Person We’re Looking For</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are an excellent writer.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You can take a complicated conversation and turn it into a clear product definition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong product judgment and are comfortable making reasonable decisions when requirements are incomplete.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You understand that a customer request is not automatically a product requirement.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are technically curious and capable of participating meaningfully in discussions with software engineers, systems engineers, operators, and external partners.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You naturally ask questions like:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">What problem are we actually trying to solve?</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Who needs this capability?</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">What should happen in this edge case?</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">What does the operator see?</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">What state is the system actually in?</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">How will we know this works?</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Is this a product decision, an engineering decision, or a customer preference?</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are highly organized, but organization is a means to an end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your real job is creating clarity and moving product decisions forward.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Particularly Valuable Experience</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with any of the following would be especially valuable:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical product management</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Complex B2B software</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Command-and-control systems</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Aerospace or defense</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Robotics or autonomous systems</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mission planning</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Geospatial software</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Systems engineering</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Government programs</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational testing</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Requirements development</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What This Role Is Not</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is not a project coordinator role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It is not a Scrum Master role.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It is not an administrative Product Operations position.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It is not someone whose primary contribution is scheduling meetings, maintaining Jira, or writing meeting minutes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Those activities may occasionally be necessary, but they are secondary.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The primary contribution is:</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>understanding product problems and defining excellent solutions.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Success After 90 Days</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You are independently drafting product specifications for bounded Legion features.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer and operator feedback is consistently translated into clear product requirements.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product meetings result in updated specifications, decisions, and actionable follow-up.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Head of Product can delegate meaningful feature-definition work to you.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Product Design receives clearer inputs and can move faster.</p></li></ul><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Important product decisions and rationale are documented and traceable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>ITAR requirement</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">To conform to U.S. Government export regulations, applicant must be a U.S. citizen, lawful permanent resident of the U.S., protected individual as defined by 8 U.S.C. 1324b(a)(3), or eligible to obtain the required authorizations from the U.S. Department of State.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Swarm Aero is an equal opportunity employer. We value diverse backgrounds and experiences and make employment decisions without regard to race, religion, national origin, gender, sexual orientation, age, veteran status, or disability.<br /><br /><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Meaningful equity in a high-growth defense technology company</p></li><li>