lenging conventional approaches and turning advanced technologies into real-world impact.</p><p>As a Sales Manager (m/f/d), you will play a key role in expanding our market presence across Germany and Europe. You will work closely with management, technical experts, and our international teams to bring sustainable, future-proof solutions to industries, municipalities, utilities, and partner networks.</p><p> </p><p><strong>Your Responsibilities</strong></p><ul><li><p>Drive and further develop our sales strategy in line with the <strong>re:think water</strong> mission</p></li><li><p>Identify new market segments, applications, and business opportunities in PFAS treatment and water technologies</p></li><li><p>Manage and grow key accounts in industry, municipalities, and partner networks</p></li><li><p>Build long-term customer relationships at decision-maker level</p></li><li><p>Participate in customer meetings, technical presentations, negotiations, and tenders</p></li><li><p>Support proposal development and the preparation of technical solution concepts</p></li><li><p>Monitor market trends and competitors and translate insights into concrete actions</p></li><li><p>Represent the Cornelsen Group at trade fairs, conferences, and industry events</p></li></ul><p> </p><p><strong>Your Profile</strong></p><ul><li><p>Degree in industrial engineering, environmental engineering, process engineering, business administration, or a comparable field</p></li><li><p>Several years of sales experience, ideally in water treatment, environmental technology, chemicals, or plant engineering</p></li><li><p>Experience handling complex technical projects and public or private tenders</p></li><li><p>Existing network in industry, municipalities, or utilities is a plus</p></li><li><p>Hands-on mindset, high mobility, and genuine enthusiasm for customer interaction</p></li><li><p>Entrepreneurial thinking, initiative, and strong results orientation</p></li><li><p>Confident communication and negotiation skills at C-level</p></li><li><p>Business-fluent German and English; additional European languages are an advantage</p></li></ul><p> </p><p><strong>What We Offer</strong></p><ul><li><p>A role with real impact in a future-critical technology field</p></li><li><p>An innovative, family-like work environment with short decision paths</p></li><li><p>International exposure through locations in Germany, the Netherlands, the UK, Sweden, and the USA</p></li><li><p>Diverse projects and plenty of room for your own ideas</p></li><li><p>Attractive compensation package including performance-based bonus</p></li><li><p>Corporate benefits, JobRad, and private pension options</p></li><li><p>The opportunity to actively shape the growth of a dynamic business area</p></li></ul><p> </p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/cornelsen-umwelttechnologie-gmbh/sales-manager-dach-region-essen-175620","tags":["Management","Team Leader"],"job_types":["Permanent employment (unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag)","manager"],"location":"Essen","created_at":1793061039},{"slug":"software-engineer-perception-gilching-137183","company_name":"Quantum-Systems GmbH","title":"Software Engineer - Perception (m/f/d)","description":"<p class="Paragraph SCXW183979662 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;">At Quantum Systems, we are building the next generation of autonomous aerial systems. The Drone Port is a key element of this vision, enabling fully autonomous launch, landing, charging, health monitoring and mission readiness of our UAV platforms.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW183979662 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;">As a <strong>Software Engineer - Perception</strong>, you will play a central role in developing the intelligence that allows the Drone Port and aircraft to interact seamlessly. You will work on perception algorithms, control systems, embedded software and sensor integration to create reliable autonomous behaviours that operate in real-world environments.</p><p class="Paragraph SCXW183979662 BCX0" style="text-align:justify;">Working closely with experts from Mechanical Engineering, Electronics, Systems Engineering Flight Controls, Embedded Software, AI and Flight Test, you will help shape one of the most advanced autonomous drone infrastructure products on the market. Your work will directly influence the future of fully autonomous BVLOS operations and scalable drone deployments worldwide.</p><blockquote><p style="text-align:justify;"><br></p></blockquote><figure><img style="width:1800px" alt="Drone Port Quantum-Systems" src="https://recruitee-main.s3.eu-central-1.amazonaws.com/uploads/v9c2tyb758/DP_Full.jpg"></figure><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><h4><strong>What is your Day to Day Mission:</strong></h4><ul><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Develop perception software for autonomous Drone Port operation.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Design and implement computer vision algorithms for precision landing, docking and localisation.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Integrate cameras and additional perception sensors into the Drone Port software stack.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Develop software for sensor processing, calibration and data synchronization.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Improve robustness of perception algorithms under varying environmental conditions.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Support the integration of perception components into the overall autonomy architecture.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Analyse test data and continuously improve perception performance based on field results.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Design, train, and optimize computer vision models for object detection, pose estimation, and related perception tasks.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Deploy models on GPU-enabled edge platforms</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Develop internal tools for testing, visualization and debugging perception pipelines.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Collaborate closely with Robotics, Embedded, Mechanical and Systems Engineering throughout the complete product development lifecycle.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Support flight and field testing of autonomous Drone Port capabilities.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Contribute to software architecture, code quality and engineering best practices</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Support flight and field testing of autonomous Drone Port capabilities.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Contribute to software architecture, coding standards and engineering best practices.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW142685783 BCX0">Mentor junior engineers and actively contribute to the technical growth of the robotics team.</p></li></ul> <br> <h4><strong><br></strong></h4><h4><strong>What you bring to the team:</strong><br></h4><ul><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW11552966 BCX0">Bachelor's or Master's degree in Computer Science, Robotics, Electrical Engineering or a related discipline.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW11552966 BCX0">First professional experience, internships or university projects in robotics, computer vision or autonomous systems.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW11552966 BCX0">Strong programming skills in Python.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW11552966 BCX0">Solid understanding of deep learning fundamentals (CNNs, transformers)</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW11552966 BCX0">Hands-on experience developing object detection and pose estimation models.</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW11552966 BCX0">Experience with PyTorch</p></li><li><p class="Paragraph SCXW11552966 BCX0">Experience with OpenCV or comparable computer vision frameworks.</p></li