are-in-the-Loop) systems, measurement equipment, control interfaces, and test benches.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Analyze test results and failures across software, firmware, electronics, and test hardware.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Support traceability from requirements to test cases, verification results, and validation evidence.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Collaborate closely with firmware, electronics, product, and quality teams to improve test methods, coverage, and reliability.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Help shape test processes that scale from development testing to release validation and production-oriented testing.</span></p></li></ul> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A degree in electrical engineering, computer science, mechatronics, embedded systems, or a comparable field</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Solid understanding of electrical engineering and embedded systems</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Programming experience in Python, C#, or C++; experience with more than one is a strong plus</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Experience with automated testing, test frameworks, lab equipment, HiL (Hardware-in-the-Loop) setups, or hardware-related test environments</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Ability to debug complex issues across software, firmware, hardware, and test infrastructure</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">A structured, thorough, and quality-oriented way of working</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Hands-on mentality and willingness to work directly with devices, test benches, and measurement setups</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Good communication skills in English</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#121317">Qualification as Elektrofachkraft (EFK), or willingness to develop further in this area, is an advantage</spa