unch and iteration. You’ll ship AI products that enterprise customers rely on.</li><li>Stay close to the product: test, refine and pressure-test our agents, and understand how prompts, context and evaluations shape quality.</li><li>Spend real time with customers. Uncover requirements, turn noisy feedback into clear priorities and become a trusted partner to their business.</li><li>Build the product function. Define how we discover, prioritise, ship and measure, and lay the foundations for a future product team.</li><li>Work with GTM on positioning and join sales conversations where product insight wins deals.</li></ul><br><br><strong>Who You Are</strong><br><br><ul><li>5+ years in product management or a closely related role (founder, early operator, consulting into product), with a strong record of shipping.</li><li>A startup operator at heart. You’ve done your best work at early-stage companies, ideally as one of the first product hires or as a founder. Experience only at large corporates won’t be the right fit for this role.</li><li>A strong all-rounder, as comfortable setting strategy as writing a detailed spec, debugging an edge case or jumping on a sales call.</li><li>Exceptional product sense and user empathy. You look past the surface of a feature request to find the root problem.</li><li>Technically curious. You don’t need a CS degree or coding skills, but you’re confident working with engineers and exploring what AI can and can’t do.</li><li>A clear communicator who uses both qualitative and quantitative reasoning to make and explain decisions.</li><li>Based in Berlin or ready to relocate.</li><li>Fluent in English and German (required for our customer base).</li><li>Nice to have: B2B or enterprise software experience (strongly preferred), hands-on work with AI/LLM products, or exposure to public sector or regulated markets.</li></ul><br><br><strong>You’ll Thrive If</strong><br><br><ul><li>You love building from 0 to 1. You don’t need a roadmap handed to you, and you enjoy creating structure where there is none.</li><li>You move fast and are energised by an intense, ambitious environment.</li><li>You have a “no task is too small” mindset and lead by doing.</li><li>You love being in the office and believe in-person collaboration drives speed.</li></ul><br><br><strong>What’s In It For You</strong><br><br><ul><li>Ownership from day one. You’ll define the product, with direct access to the founders and zero red tape.</li><li>A role that grows with you. As the company scales, so do your scope and your team.</li><li>Shared upside: top-of-market compensation and generous equity.</li><li>A mission that matters. You won’t be optimising ad clicks. You’ll be helping businesses and the public sector cut waste on a huge scale.</li></ul><br><br><strong>Our Process</strong><br><br><ul><li><strong>Review:</strong> All applications reviewed within 5 days.</li><li><strong>Intro call:</strong> 30 minutes on your background and motivations.</li><li><strong>Product deep dive (remote):</strong> 1 hour on your product thinking and problem-solving.</li><li><strong>On-site (half day):</strong> Work through a real product use case with the team, followed by 1:1s with Engineering and GTM.</li><li><strong>Offer:</strong> A quick final decision and transparent feedback straight after the on-site.</li></ul><br><br><strong>How to Apply</strong><br><br>Apply through this posting with:<br><br><ul><li>Your CV</li><li>A few lines on what excites you about this role</li><li>Optional: links to products you’ve shipped</li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.com">Jobs in Germany</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/cherry-ventures/head-of-product-berlin-59622","tags":["IT"],"job_types":["professional / experienced"],"location":"Berlin","created_at":1793025054},{"slug":"qualitatsingenieur-quality-engineer-mainz-213465","company_name":"Xylem","title":"Qualitätsingenieur / Quality Engineer (m/w/d)","des