e":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.com/jobs/companies/wesearch-personalberatung/leitung-export-key-account-management-frankfurt-am-main-301014","tags":["Management","Team Leader"],"job_types":["Unbefristeter arbeitsvertrag","teamleitung"],"location":"Frankfurt am Main","created_at":1793023268},{"slug":"senior-business-development-associate-london-90837","company_name":"Ideo","title":"Senior Business Development Associate","description":"&lt;h1&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Senior Business Development Associate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h1&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;In a Nutshell&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Senior Business Development Associates bring ideas, initiatives, and activities that help grow our business day in and day out. They join, support, and collaborate with teams focused on specific opportunities, ensuring that the pursuit of new business is rigorous, disciplined, and ethical. They collaborate closely to craft strategies and plans and set the standard for creative excellence in business development.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About IDEO London&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re a global design consultancy where curiosity, empathy, and solving complex challenges drive us. For over 40 years, we&#39;ve partnered with clients to innovate in healthcare, mobility, education, retail, and beyond. Here, every challenge is a chance to grow, connect, and create impact.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Why is this role important for IDEO&#39;s work?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Business Development is at the heart of connecting IDEO&#39;s creative capabilities with the people and organisations who need them. It&#39;s about more than winning new work. It&#39;s about understanding our clients&#39; challenges, building trusted relationships, and helping shape opportunities where human-centred design can make a meaningful difference.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Once Here You Will&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;BUSINESS DEVELOPMENT PROCESS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prioritize your time to collaborate and support the London Studio in landing project work - with new and returning clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Run pipeline meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as an IDEO ambassador and be the first touch point for new potential clients, ensuring a positive initial experience with IDEO.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead and manage opportunity qualification, owning continuity of the BD process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Involve internal leadership and designers as needed for boosts and to help determine strategic fit, frame opportunities, scope programs and articulate next steps.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Pull in director-level support as needed for advocating for client needs and negotiation support.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Finalize pitch decks, learn the industries of our client leads by conducting research and editing proposal decks, and brainstorm client deliverable options and consulting solutions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct client due diligence to help BD teams get smart and prepare for calls, creating intelligent discussion guides that help us start to build a relationship with potential clients from Day One.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Monitor and communicate market trends and themes to teams on a monthly basis that can be used to help shape our thinking and offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;REPORTING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Track quarterly goals pertaining to recognized revenue, monthly profit and yield marks, time to close, conversion rate, qualification rate, and win rate KPIs within the London Hub. Report back in the pipeline meetings, looking for ways to engage the team in the information and how they need to apply it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be familiar with metrics that point towards the health of the business and be able to assist with ad-hoc reporting needs as assigned.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prepare a monthly summary of insights and thought leadership (from IDEO and beyond), including how it applies to day-to-day business, to share with key clients as a value add.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DATA INTEGRITY&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with the Director/Enterprise team to ensure the CRM system is kept up to date, including our pipeline and pre-pipeline in Hubspot.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure that relevant documents related to BD are being stored and filed accordingly in the BD section of Google Drive (not on personal drives or Slack!).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Appropriately loop in Legal, Marketing, Finance, and other functions as needed to progress an ongoing BD process.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build and maintain lists in Hubspot and LinkedIn Sales Navigator: who are our key clients, our lapsed clients, our warm contacts, the cold contacts we want to reach? Who’s engaging with our newsletters, with our LinkedIn, etc? Provide recommendations on how we might reach out to these folks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;PROGRAM MANAGEMENT&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exercise project management tactical skills by effectively steering the BD process for new and existing work.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proactively identify and take action on the business development process and client needs based on what we’re hearing and seeing in the pipeline meetings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate meetings with potential leads, ensure prompt and adequate follow-ups, manage legal agreement workflows, coordinate proposal research across teams, and ensure continual progress to meet client deadlines.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Help the team balance meeting the needs of existing clientele with prioritizing time for proactive outreach to land new clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own and project manage lead generation activities, such as BD-specific mailers to LON Hub mailing lists.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support account planning activities to drive a proactive, consistent approach to client investment and development.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support the deployment of the right expertise and experience from within the hub team towards client pursuits&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;COMMUNICATION&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate persuasive and effective communication and presentation skills along with the confidence to command a room for the client and network-building meetings or events.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Contribute to providing excellent team and client communication and collaboration that shows an understanding of leading with empathy, openness, and curiosity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Empower other team members to consistently gather and share inspiration, work, and learnings with teams and clients. This should come through leading by example as well as having a knowledge management system where folks can exchange and store content.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen existing assets and develop new ones in collaboration with subject matter experts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with LON Hub Marketing to stay abreast of competitors and any impact that industry and economic changes and movements might have on our go to market positioning and offer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NETWORK BUILDING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrate knowledge of the different approaches across each of our three offer sets, and understand the different areas of expertise of our design disciplines to confidently speak to our capabilities in the market.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Build cross-discipline relationships across IDEO in order to effectively help generate and capture written, verbal and visual input from IDEO leadership and design teams to potential client leads.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cultivate your internal networks as well as you professional networks virtually on social media channels and live at education and industry-related associations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support top-of-funnel growth activity including working with the Executive Director of Growth, Marketing and portfolio teams to translate targeting priorities into actionable prospect audiences and lists for campaigns, events, roadshows and other market-facing activity.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;EXPLORE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strengthen your foundational BD skills and capabilities, using your learning budget intentionally to build on growth opportunities identified with your business lead.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Gain an understanding of GenAI and how it can support and improve the BD process, from generating client intelligence to scoring our RFP responses.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support special projects as needed and provide support on other processes and projects outside the immediate area of responsibilities as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assist with internal programs and initiatives to improve organizational BD efforts, as required.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be an active member of the London community, coming into the office as needed, playing a role in our core rituals, such as Tuesday Morning Meetings, participating in SASU, and attending Hub gatherings.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;We&#39;re looking for someone with&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;SKILLS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Minimum of 3-5 years of relevant experience in client relationship management and business development, preferably within a creative environment and/or design consultancy.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Project management skills with proven ability to prioritize tasks, keep momentum and develop timelines, involve and engage stakeholders, and maintain empathy for both internal and client teams.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;The ability to create and deliver presentations, proposals, and other assets.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Data literacy: fluent in G-suite (slides, docs, and sheets), Workday, CRM, and translating quantitative outputs into actionable qualitative insights for the business.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exceptional writing and communication skills to effectively and efficiently bridge between IDEO and its clients.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong presentation and writing skills&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to conduct and synthesize research&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Attention to Detail: Demonstrates concern for the details and their impact on the larger picture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with a wide range of market analysis tools, data sets, and benchmarks.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort determining next steps in ambiguous situations with limited direction.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ready to pitch in on tasks, big or small. Volunteer and helper mindset.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Desire to collaborate across various design disciplines&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take chances without being afraid to fail and learn along the way&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Insatiable curiosity to learn more about businesses, industries, markets, and what drives them&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;MINDSET&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ground in Self-Awareness: Reflect on your biases and lenses to be more inclusive.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Show Curiosity: Question accepted norms to make room to learn from more diverse voices.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lean into Vulnerability: Build trust by being open.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ask for and give consistent and timely feedback on personal performance.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Be optimistic&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborate&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Embrace ambiguity&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Talk Less, Do more&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Learn from failure&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Make others successful&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What does IDEO offer you?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Innovation and creativity:&lt;/strong&gt; Dive into a variety of projects from creating breakthrough digital products and experiences, to designing new customer interactions, to building innovation capabilities – working alongside talented individuals across disciplines.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Learning and growth:&lt;/strong&gt; Whether it’s strengthening your project leadership, deepening your interaction design craft or exploring new technologies, we’re here to support your journey.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Community and well-being:&lt;/strong&gt; Collaboration and community are central to what we do. We foster moments for creativity, connection, and reflection, respecting the need for work-life balance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Projects with purpose:&lt;/strong&gt; We partner with clients to use design as a means of realising their purpose and making a positive impact. We work &#39;upstream,&#39; from defining the problem, designing possible solutions, and exploring what, why and how they might be brought to life.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Compensation&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;£55,000 - 60,000 GBP, depending on experience&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Location&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;London, UK&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Some Previous Projects To Check Out&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;To get a flavour of the work we do in London, take a look at these case studies:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/works/sage&quot;&gt;Climate action for SMBs&lt;/a&gt; – Designing a strategy and experience to help Sage’s SMB customers transition to net zero.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/case-study/femsa&quot;&gt;Redefining retail with FEMSA&lt;/a&gt; – Designing Spin Premia, a digital loyalty experience connecting everyday shopping at OXXO with rewards and services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.ideo.com/works/h-and-m&quot;&gt;Sustainable packaging system&lt;/a&gt; – Helping H&amp;amp;M increase their sustainability and growth, by designing and scaling a universal packaging system for all of their brands.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Commitment to Diversity&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At IDEO, we are committed to the work of advancing diversity, equity, and inclusion within our organisation and in the world. Our purpose of having disproportionate, world-changing impact through design is directly connected to our ability to bring many different perspectives to the table. This applies to our candidates, the people we hire, the clients and customers we serve, and the communities we learn from in our research.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a human-centred organisation, we are committed to working with and designing for people of every race, ethnicity, gender identity, sexual orientation, age, socio-economic status, physical ability or attribute, religion, national origin, or political belief. We recognize that this commitment requires ongoing work and sustained attention, as well as adaptation to new insights and best practices&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Application Requirements And Instructions&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you identify with our values, are excited about great design, and would like to contribute to our community, we would love to see your CV, a cover letter and examples of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/ideo/senior-business-development-associate-london-90837","tags":["Business Development"],"job_types":[],"location":"London","created_at":1793062522},{"slug":"social-media-content-manager-london-100707","company_name":"Zilch","title":"Social Media & Content Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we are:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're one of Europe's fastest-growing fintech companies – on a mission to create the world's most empowering way to pay.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched the product in 2020 and achieved double unicorn status, valued at $2 billion, and since then have taken on more than 6 million customers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our mission is to become the best way to pay for anything, anywhere and say goodbye to credit costs for everyone. This is huge. Want to join us?</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the role.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Zilch is looking for an experienced social media and content manager to help shape how we show up online. You’ll lead our LinkedIn presence and manage content for the company blog, turning company, product, partnership and customer stories into clear, engaging material.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role. You’ll be well-connected across the business, find stories, plan what to share, write and edit content, publish it, and learn from how it performs. You’ll help Zilch build a consistent presence throughout the year, not just around major announcements, and support senior leaders to share their ideas and expertise.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">LinkedIn experience is essential. The role also covers the company blog and may extend to other channels as Zilch’s needs and opportunities evolve. As a payments business, accuracy and good judgement matter: you’ll need to make complex topics easy to understand without losing the detail.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Day to day responsibilities.</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the day-to-day running of Zilch’s LinkedIn presence, including the content plan, publishing schedule and performance reviews.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Translate Zilch’s communications objectives into editorial priorities and content plans, making day-to-day decisions within agreed messaging and approval guidelines.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage the company blog: develop story ideas, write and edit articles, coordinate contributions and keep content up to date.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Write and edit clear, engaging posts, explainers, customer and partner stories, and other content for social channels and the blog.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Find useful stories in Zilch’s products, partnerships, people and business updates, and work with colleagues to bring them to life.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help senior leaders develop a confident, authentic voice on LinkedIn. This may include drafting posts, articles and commentary on their behalf.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Turn company announcements and business milestones into a range of useful content for the blog, LinkedIn and other relevant channels.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with design, video and other teams to create content in formats that suit the story and the audience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track what people respond to, report on results and use these insights to improve results against channel objectives and performance measures agreed with communications leadership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep an eye on relevant conversations and trends, and bring forward timely ideas that fit Zilch.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll sit within the communications team and work closely with Marketing, Product, Commercial and Legal teams to find stories, check facts and coordinate content.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Establish and improve editorial workflows, briefing and approval processes, and content standards, working with Legal and other teams to ensure accuracy and timely publication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Guide colleagues who contribute content, sharing feedback and practical advice to strengthen writing quality and consistency.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help develop Zilch’s presence on other channels where there is a good opportunity to reach the right audience. This could include existing or new social platforms, video, newsletters or other formats.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Develop relationships and support work with creators, influencers or finance voices when it fits a campaign.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What we’re looking for...</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Around 5-10 years’ experience in social media, content or editorial roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong, hands-on experience managing and creating content for LinkedIn. You can show how you’ve built a consistent company or executive presence on the platform.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent writing and editing skills, with examples of work that is clear, engaging and well judged.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience planning and delivering content from idea to publication, including managing an editorial calendar or blog.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The ability to explain financial, technical or regulatory topics in plain English while keeping them accurate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Good editorial judgement and close attention to detail, especially when working with sensitive or complex subjects.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A creative flair for developing great content and the ability to spot trends and jump on them early</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong organisation skills and the ability to manage several pieces of work at once.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confidence working with senior leaders and colleagues across different teams to find and develop stories.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">The drive to make connections with finfluencers in the industry and collaborate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with other social channels or content formats is useful, and you’re open to exploring new ones as Zilch’s needs develop.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">A background in finance, fintech or technology would be preferable. Experience in another consumer-facing or regulated industry would also be relevant.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /><strong>Benefits.</strong><br /><strong><br />Compensation &amp; Savings:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Pension scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Death in Service scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Income Protection.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Permanent employees enjoy access to our Share Options Scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5% back on in-app purchases.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">£200 for WFH Setup.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Health &amp; Wellbeing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Medical Insurance including;</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">GP consultations (video, telephone or face-to-face).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prescribed medication.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In-patient, day-patient and out-patient care.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mental health support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optical, dental &amp; audiological cover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Physiotherapy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Advanced cancer cover.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Menopause support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee Assistance Programme including:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited mental health sessions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">24/7 remote GP &amp; physiotherapy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">24/7 helpline for emotional &amp; practical support.</p></li></ul></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Savings &amp; discounts on everyday shopping.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1:1 personalised well-being consultations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Gym membership discounts.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Family Friendly Policies:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced maternity pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced paternity pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced adoption pay.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced shared parental leave.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Learning &amp; Development:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional Qualifications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Professional Memberships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learning Suite for e-courses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Internal Training Programmes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">FCA &amp; Regulatory training.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Workplace Perks:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid working: office-based Monday, Wednesday, and Thursday; remote working Tuesday and Friday</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Casual dress code.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Workplace socials.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Healthy snacks.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/zilch/social-media-content-manager-london-100707","tags":["Communications"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zilch UK","created_at":1793061613},{"slug":"accounts-assistant-london-291459","company_name":"Fanvue.com","title":"Accounts Assistant","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>💰 £40,000–£45,000</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>📍 Salary based on London. Other locations may vary.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Fanvue is one of the fastest-growing creator monetisation platforms globally. We're an AI-powered, creator-first platform helping creators connect, engage, and earn directly from their audiences at scale. Following our recent Series A, Fanvue has surpassed $200m+ in annual recurring revenue, with triple-digit year-on-year growth, supporting hundreds of thousands of creators and millions of fans worldwide.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Behind the product is a finance function that needs to be as fast and reliable as the platform itself.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🎯 The Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're hiring an <strong>Assistant Accountant</strong> to own the accounting engine of the finance team: the ledger, the month-end close, and the admin that keeps both clean. Our day-to-day transaction processing is supported by an outsourced bookkeeping partner. You'll own the quality of that work, the reconciliations behind it, and everything between a receipt landing and a number reaching the board pack.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Everything else in finance, reporting, forecasting and investor diligence depends on the ledger being right. You'll make sure it is: reviewing what goes in, reconciling what comes out, and closing the month on time. About a quarter of the role is finance admin. It means running the invoice inbox, chasing receipts and keeping supplier records clean, and it's what keeps the numbers right.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🚀 What You'll Do</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Ledger and close</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Review and own the ledger in Xero, including our outsourced bookkeepers' work on coding, supplier bills and daily bank reconciliations across GBP, USD and EUR accounts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare month-end journals, accruals and prepayments, and the balance sheet reconciliations behind them, so we close by working day 5 with our Finance Manager</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Keep intercompany balances with our US entity reconciled</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Reconcile payroll, PAYE and pension control accounts to Rippling each month</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare the UK VAT return in Xero for review</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Prepare year-end schedules and answer queries from our external accountants and auditors</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Finance admin and communication</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Run the invoice inbox, logging, chasing and routing supplier invoices so nothing reaches the ledger without a document</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Chase receipts and missing context from colleagues for card spend, and keep receipt compliance high</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain supplier records and support onboarding, including verifying bank details before anything is paid</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be the first point of contact for finance questions from the wider team</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>👀 Who You Are</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">2 to 4 years in a finance team or accounting practice, with at least one month-end close owned end to end</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AAT qualified, or studying towards or part-qualified in ACCA, CIMA or ACA. We'll support your studies</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Confident in Xero or similar cloud accounting software, and comfortable with large data sets in Excel or Google Sheets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience with multi-currency reconciliations and high transaction volumes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear, friendly written communication. You'll chase people across the company and keep it pleasant</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fintech, marketplace or payments experience is a strong plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>✨ You'll Thrive Here If</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A fully reconciled balance sheet gives you real satisfaction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You chase people for answers instead of waiting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You see the admin as part of getting the numbers right, not a distraction from it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're comfortable in a startup where things move fast around you, even if your work is methodical</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to grow into a management accountant or financial controller role as the team scales</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>⚠️ You'll Struggle Here If</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You want to work only on the numbers and see chasing colleagues for receipts as beneath the role</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You need heavy supervision or detailed instructions for every task</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're not comfortable working with high transaction volumes daily</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>🌍 Why Join Fanvue?</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sunday Times Best Places to Work, two years running. We don't just say we have great culture, we prove it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Your work has immediate, visible impact. When the books are clean, the whole company moves faster, leadership gets reliable numbers, and investor conversations go smoothly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A clear path to grow, with study support and room to step up as the finance team expands</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fanvue supports hundreds of thousands of creators and millions of fans globally. The problems you solve here are real and immediate</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fully remote with unlimited PTO, flexible working hours, a London office and WeWork access when you want it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Salary reviews every six months, we don't wait for annual cycles to recognise your growth</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Travel and office budgets for team off-sites or kitting out your home setup</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A benefits package we're actively building out, including gym memberships and apps</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A culture built on innovation, speed, excellence, ownership and transparency</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>⭐ Fanvue is for Everyone</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We know that diverse teams build better products. Even if you do not meet every requirement, we encourage you to apply. Potential, mindset, and ambition matter just as much as experience.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/fanvuecom/accounts-assistant-london-291459","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Hybrid (London)","created_at":1793061612},{"slug":"operations-lead-london-25269","company_name":"Magentic","title":"Operations Lead","description":"<h1></h1><h2>About Magentic</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Magentic, we're building the next generation of AI agents to transform how the world's largest companies manage procurement and supply chains.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're tackling a $3 trillion market, building AI systems that can autonomously manage complex procurement workflows and help make global manufacturing supply chains more resilient.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Backed by Sequoia and Felicis, we've brought together an exceptional team with experience from OpenAI, Meta, Revolut, NASA and McKinsey.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're growing quickly, solving challenging problems and building something with the potential to change how critical industries operate. It's an exciting time to join, early enough to make an huge impact and help shape what comes next.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About the Role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for an experienced Operations Lead to play a key role in shaping how Magentic operates as we grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is the perfect opportunity for someone who is proactive, independent and comfortable taking ownership and making decisions. You'll be pragmatic and commercially minded, with a focus on delivering real impact rather than overcomplicating things. You'll thrive in a fast-paced startup environment, know how to balance competing priorities and be confident finding solutions that work for the business as we grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">It’s a wide ranging, highly collaborative role that will interact with the whole business: you'll work across people operations, IT and tooling, legal and compliance, alongside leading projects that improve how we work across the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What You'll Do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of key People Operations processes, helping create a great employee experience as we grow.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Shape how we use internal systems and tooling, finding smarter ways to work and opportunities to introduce automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Take ownership of legal and compliance operations, working with external advisers to ensure we're set up for success as we scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive high-impact projects, working closely with teams across the business to evolve our ways of working as we scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and introduce new processes that make a genuine difference to how we operate, bringing together people, tools and data to support our growth.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What We're Looking For</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5–6+ years' experience in Operations or a similar generalist role, including experience leading on one of the key areas (people operations, legal, compliance or IT).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in high-growth startups is a must.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A whizz AI, tooling and automation.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong attention to detail and organisational skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Compensation and Benefits</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Magentic, we recognise and reward the talent that drives our success. We offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Competitive Equity</strong>: play a real part in Magentic’s upside.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary: £100,000 - £110,000 per annum</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private healthcare</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Hybrid London HQ</strong> (4 days in the office).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Company provided meals</strong> at the office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Monthly “Social budget”</strong> to spend getting to know your colleagues (coffee, food, activities, etc.)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work from anywhere 4 weeks out of the year</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Salary sacrifice pension and nursery schemes</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Annual team retreat</strong>—a fully-funded off-site to recharge, bond, and build.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Our Interview Process</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We can move quickly through these stages, so let us know if you have any timelines we need to meet.</p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Initial</strong> <strong>call</strong> <strong>(30 mins)</strong>: this first step is an opportunity for you to hear more about Magentic and the role, and for us to learn more about how your experience aligns with the role.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Skills interview (45 mins):</strong> in this step, we'll ask you to prepare a presentation and take Q&amp;A.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>In-person interview (half-day, paid):</strong> for the final step, we invite you to come meet the team in-person. We find this is the best way for candidates to get a sense of what working at Magentic is like. This day will include a culture interview, founder interview and a presentation task / discussion with the team.</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2><strong>Equal Opportunities and Accommodations Statement</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Magentic, our mission i