<p><span data-sheets-root="1">At Wolt, we create technology that brings joy, simplicity and earnings to the neighborhoods of the world. In 2014 we started with delivery of restaurant food. Now we're building the delivery of (almost) everything and you'll find us in over 500 cities in 30 countries around the world. In 2022 we joined forces with DoorDash and together we keep on dreaming big and expanding across the globe.<br><br>Working at Wolt isn't always easy, but it's definitely exciting. Here you'll learn more, build more, and ship more than in most other companies. You'll be challenged a lot, but also have a lot of fun on the way. So, if you're a self-starter with drive and entrepreneurial spirit, this could be the ride of your life.</span></p></div><h2>About the Team</h2>
<p>Our Infrastructure teams build the foundation that engineers at Wolt, Deliveroo, and DoorDash build on: the compute, cloud, and networking capabilities that enable Engineering teams to develop, deploy, and run services at global scale. The EU Compute team has a specific focus on provisioning, scaling, and the efficient operation of GPU infrastructure for AI and ML workloads. This is an emerging space with plenty of greenfield opportunities.</p>
<p>We're looking for a Staff Engineer to be a hands-on technical leader for this infrastructure work that crosses team and brand boundaries. You'll set direction for the platform, turn complex problems into deliverable plans, write and review production code, and help other engineers make sound decisions. It's an exciting time to join: we're building a global platform and the choices made now will shape how engineers across the company ship for years.</p>
<h2>What you'll be doing</h2>
<p>You'll own some of the hardest infrastructure problems in the company and make the platform easier to operate and safer to build on. We're determined to build great platform products and user experiences, and you'll be pivotal in making this reality.</p>
<h3>Day-to-day in this role you'll:</h3>
<ul>
<li>Set technical direction for shared AWS and Kubernetes infrastructure, balancing reliability, security, developer experience, and cost.</li>
<li>Lead substantial initiatives from design through rollout and operation, coordinating dependencies and decisions across Wolt, Deliveroo and DoorDash, focusing on workloads targeting GPUs.</li>
<li>Evolve Kubernetes clusters, cloud networking, identity, and infrastructure provisioning to support growing and varied workloads.</li>
<li>Build reusable Terraform patterns and self-service tooling that help teams provision infrastructure safely and consistently.</li>
<li>Improve deployment and operational practices, including GitOps, observability, capacity planning, incident response and recovery.</li>
<li>Use production signals and developer feedback to find platform friction, choose where to invest and measure whether changes actually help.</li>
<li>Assist with supporting the platform, with deep focus on GPU infrastructure, as well as broad focus on compute in general.</li>
<li>Gracefully sunset legacy infrastructure and tooling, and create strategies to reduce toil.</li>
<li>Mentor engineers through design reviews, implementation and incidents, raising the quality of infrastructure work across teams.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Our humble expectations</h2>
<ul>
<li>Deep experience building and operating Kubernetes and AWS infrastructure in production. Familiarity with GPU workloads and orchestration is a plus.</li>
<li>Strong software engineering skills: you use Go, Python or a similar language to build maintainable tools and automation.</li>
<li>Experience with infrastructure as code (we use Terraform) and with designing systems that other engineering teams depend on.</li>
<li>A track record of leading complex technical work across teams, including architectural decisions, delivery, and operational follow-through. You have the breadth to collaborate and design across team and domain boundaries, and the depth to have hands-on impact.</li>
<li>Strong judgment on trade-offs in distributed systems, networking, security, reliability, and cloud cost.</li>
<li>Clear communication, and the ability to bring people together around a practical technical direction.</li>
</ul>
<h2>What we offer</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Scope and influence.</strong> Shape infrastructure used globally, while staying close to the engineering. Your work will help product teams ship services with greater ease and confidence.</li>
<li><strong>Real problems at global scale.</strong> Multi-cluster Kubernetes, AI / ML workloads, cloud networking, GitOps, and progressive delivery across a global company.</li>
<li><strong>Autonomy and ownership.</strong> Set direction and see it through from design to operation, with the backing of a global engineering organisation spanning Europe and the US.</li>
<li><strong>Growth.</strong> Room to expand your scope, whether through deeper technical leadership or broader cross-domain influence.</li>
<li><strong>Great people.</strong> Work with talented engineers and leaders in a diverse, international environment, mentoring and learning from others.</li>
</ul>
<p><iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/GoL541_xj9w" width="560" height="314"></iframe></p><div class="content-conclusion"><h2><span data-sheets-root="1">Our Commitment to Diversity and Inclusion</span></h2>
<p><span data-sheets-root="1">We're committed to growing and empowering a more inclusive community within our company, industry, and cities. That's why we hire and cultivate diverse teams of people from all backgrounds, experiences, and perspectives. We believe that true innovation happens when everyone has room at the table and the tools, resources, and opportunity to excel.</span></p>
<p><em>Beware of recruitment scams: DoorDash, Deliveroo, and Wolt will never ask you to pay money or share sensitive financial information during hiring — learn more about our legitimate recruiting process at <span class="_80om1qgj _1e0c1nu9" data-testid="smart-link-draggable-inline"><span class="loader-wrapper"><span class="hover-card-trigger-wrapper" data-testid="hover-card-trigger-wrapper"><a class="_1yt4x7n9 _2rko1ssi _v56415x0 _1e0c1nu9 _16d9qvcn _syaz13af _1rkwglyw _4cvx1w55 _19itia51 _bfhkhp5a _1a3b18uv _4fprglyw _5goinqa1 _9oik18uv _1bnxglyw _jf4cnqa1 _1nrm18uv _c2waglyw _1iohnqa1 _uizt1kdv _nt751r31 _49pcglyw _1hvw1o36 _1372tlke _7ehiw5lj _1j5pglyw _1di615s3" href="https://careersatdoordash.com/recruitment-scam-awareness" data-testid="inline-card-resolved-view"><span class="_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw _o5721jtm _1nmz9jpi _16d9qvcn _ca0qv77o _u5f31b66 _n3tdv77o _19bv1b66" data-testid="inline-card-icon-and-title"><span class="_19itglyw _vchhusvi _r06hglyw">Recruitment Scam Awareness - DoorDash</span></span></a></span></span></span> .</em></p></div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/wolt-english/staff-engineer-eu-infrastructure-london-91046","tags":[],"job_types":[],"location":"London, England, United Kingdom","created_at":1793054726},{"slug":"golang-backend-engineer-financial-product-fraud-london-14945","company_name":"Deliveroo ","title":"Golang Backend Engineer, Financial Product Fraud","description":"<div class="content-intro"><p><strong>Our Global Structure</strong></p>
<p><br>Deliveroo is now part of DoorDash, bringing together teams with even greater reach, scale, and ambition. Depending on your role, you may collaborate with teammates, systems, and leaders across DoorDash and Wolt. Together, we're unlocking new possibilities as one global team.</p></div><h2>Your job is to make sure every payout and transaction lands with the right person.</h2>
<p>We have spent years getting very good at protecting the things a marketplace has always had to protect: checkout fraud, account takeover, courier abuse. But we are no longer only a marketplace. We now issue banking products, lend to merchants, move instant payouts to couriers, and collect cash on the doorstep. Every one of those is a new way for money to leave the platform.</p>
<p>This is a new team, and it owns that surface: fraud wherever money moves through the platform. Who receives it, who lends it, who collects it, and who holds it in a financial account. Think instant payout rails, merchant cash advances, and platform-issued banking and earned-wage products serving millions of couriers and merchants. These are live loss surfaces, and the volume grows with every financial product we launch.</p>
<p>We are now looking for a <strong>Backend Engineer (Golang)</strong> to build that protection. You will design and ship real-time detection and automated enforcement for our financial products across DoorDash, Wolt, and Deliveroo. The work is high-throughput, low-latency, and unusually consequential: a rule you ship on Monday can stop a serious loss by Friday. It is also close to greenfield, so you will be setting the patterns every future financial product inherits on day one.</p>
<p>This role will be based in <strong>London</strong>, <strong>UK</strong> as one of the founding engineering roles in our London hub, working closely with our teams in Helsinki and Berlin.</p>
<h3>What you'll do:</h3>
<ul>
<li>Build and maintain high-throughput, low-latency backend services in Go that score financial events in real time, including payout enrollments, bank account links, credit applications, and account-to-account transfers.</li>
<li>Design fraud detection and automated enforcement for our financial products end to end: from signal collection through to the decision that blocks a fraudulent payout.</li>
<li>Build on and extend our shared fraud decisioning platform, so signals, rules, and models work across all three of our brands instead of being rebuilt three times.</li>
<li>Partner closely with risk analysts, data scientists, and product managers to turn observed fraud patterns into shipped detection, and to know when a rule, a model, or a product change is the right answer.</li>
<li>Work across team boundaries with our account security, payments fraud, and financial product teams. We build on their signals rather than rebuild them, so clean interfaces matter.</li>
<li>Contribute to architectural discussions and technical decisions as we establish the fraud infrastructure baseline for financial products, with support from senior engineers on the team.</li>
<li>Write well-tested, observable code and help the team hold a high quality bar. In fraud, a silent failure is a loss event.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Our expectations:</h2>
<ul>
<li>3 to 6 years of professional software engineering experience, including backend services you have shipped and owned in production.</li>
<li>1+ years of production experience in Golang, or strong experience in another backend language and real enthusiasm for picking Go up quickly.</li>
<li>A working understanding of low-latency, high-throughput distributed systems. Real-time decisioning comes with a latency budget, and you are keen to learn to build inside one.</li>
<li>Hands-on experience with SQL and/or NoSQL databases, and some exposure to event-driven architectures (Kafka or similar).</li>
<li>Willingness to operate what you build, including a share of on-call, with a pragmatic approach to reliability.</li>
<li>Uses AI tooling in day-to-day development and can critically evaluate its output for correctness and quality.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>Nice to have</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>Experience in fraud, risk, payments, lending, or financial crime, especially money movement fraud, bank account linking fraud, payout abuse, or lending fraud.</li>
<li>Experience with rules engines, real-time feature stores, or ML model serving in a decisioning path.</li>
<li>Background in Kotlin, Java, Python, or Node.js alongside Go.</li>
<li>Familiarity with cloud infrastructure (AWS, GCP).</li>
<li>Experience working across multiple brands, regions, or regulatory regimes.</li>
</ul>
<p><strong>What we value</strong></p>
<ul>
<li>A product-oriented mindset. You think beyond the ticket, understand the "why" behind the work, and take a high level of responsibility for outcomes rather than output.</li>
<li>Comfort with ambiguity. This is a new team on a new surface; parts of the charter are still being drawn, and you will help draw them.</li>
<li>A track record of owning a project or feature end to end, especially in fast-paced environments.</li>
<li>Clear and proactive communication, with a collaborative spirit. We work across three companies and several time zones, so we move fast, but we succeed together.</li>
<li>An adversarial instinct. The best fraud engineers enjoy thinking like the attacker.</li>
</ul><div class="content-conclusion"><p><strong>Diversity, Equity and Inclusion</strong><br><br>At Deliveroo, we know that a great workplace reflects the world around us and that true diversity and inclusion make us stronger, more creative, and better at what we do. We're committed to fostering an environment where everyone can do their best work and feel they belong.</p>
<p>We believe in equality of opportunity and welcome candidates from all backgrounds regardless of age, gender, ethnicity, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, socio-economic background, religion, or belief.</p>
<p>If you have a disability or long-term health condition and need support to apply for one of our roles, or require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, you'll have the opportunity to let us know once you've submitted your application. We'll share details on how to request support so we can ensure you have a fair and equitable experience.</p>
