&lt;p&gt;For more information, visit &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=6XmzUHfuQ-i5S31_qCIpcQCQtcZ6e1ZCg-K9ZDUrOSjhU2y_ydujWqUSk1qbf0g08qVEJgBQCRrYN_rQ6s8R1bQPdaN9iF-VnAt04umDr2dE8nvrwxpZdkrAXEGT1B1W&quot;&gt;https://investors.everquote.com&lt;/a&gt; and follow on &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.globenewswire.com/Tracker?data=77BAgL1nVeMykQsQieJyMOhYF-A1vLMHTvEuCfBOEZ3y8__JO9djvQmh39yBJX6yJu8z7nHYbHDvvyVkE2tBDSmNhEC7b1rXdBhuOD6_EEW4-W-Bal3QIK35pntX1W7wpCEWJkz5Ouui49uO507CTSlujcntR_vtPWE-rgBZ5E-p2PqAuo57e5Qv4Tv6QhC-n6qQjfy6QyTWRFcSaZnBetOgWYZADxcw-o4FsA_59RFz1Jt7fklOmQ8TWFMdjowUuoeYy-eog8rwjsES_lJwEPPqVjfaCHv76iX7KX3pOhGVuO1kDfKFQNaGgpnnqIY3W8mYzPeMJEisnZ6PgV4sgO1EVe7cY0cS8JDoOc9JMsBma3kScg5NSRPdt1ZNQvAnsjfWLaj8Q0Xmg9vqEkXqhvPvYuXbpSBpuADuxOKh8Yn2rAJzPdDDRbBgVEuYzlbVwrHM27mDXBGESKq_dfkYajMWrNGjbF3dg4omuuCvDpneGp3mrnk6IMTmwiogaLCXrp6dHSw_rVHsXixipTUhAXy7Gd_5_zeuDewZ1X_4gSV-f-fuipPZ42u2YD6RiUF-mP4WAjF7yUJkbh0nMJjY0g==&quot;&gt;LinkedIn&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/everquote/software-engineer-ii-security-belfast-northern-ireland-244283","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":[],"location":"Belfast, Northern Ireland","created_at":1793051728},{"slug":"field-marketing-manager-net-new-emea-dam-london-109374","company_name":"Sitecore","title":"Field Marketing Manager - Net New EMEA (DAM)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Us:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Sitecore, our mission is to simplify how brands reach, engage, and serve people by delivering intelligent, personalised digital experiences that connect the world. We empower the world’s most iconic brands to build lifelong relationships with their customers—seamlessly, smartly, and at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the leading provider of agentic digital experience software, Sitecore brings together content, commerce, and data into one composable platform that enables brands to deliver millions of meaningful, adaptive experiences every day. Trusted by global leaders such as American Express, Porsche, Starbucks, and L’Oréal, Sitecore helps brands transform engagement through experiences that are not only personalised but predictive and dynamic.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our foundation is our people—a diverse, passionate, and collaborative global team spanning over 25 countries. We believe that every experience matters, and that belief starts with how we work together. Our values—empathy, accountability, clarity, and growth—guide how we lead, innovate, and connect. They are the behaviours that bring our mission and vision to life, every day, in every interaction.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As we continue to evolve, we are actively cultivating AI skills across our teams to unlock new levels of creativity, efficiency, and insight. From engineering to customer experience, AI capabilities are becoming integral to how we design, build, and deliver the next generation of digital experiences.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Learn more at <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="http://Sitecore.com"><u>Sitecore.com</u></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the Role:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sitecore is seeking a dynamic and results-driven Field Marketing Manager to lead Net New demand generation for Digital Asset Management (DAM) across EMEA. This role will build market awareness, create qualified pipeline, and accelerate new customer acquisition through integrated field marketing aligned with regional go-to-market priorities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will develop and execute multi-channel programs that bring the DAM value proposition to target accounts and priority industries. Working closely with the DAM team, regional sales, business development, product marketing, and campaigns, you will turn audience and market insight into measurable pipeline. The ideal candidate is entrepreneurial, commercially minded, data-driven, and comfortable operating in a fast-paced, matrixed environment.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Will Do:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strategy &amp; Planning</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and execute the Net New DAM demand generation strategy for EMEA, aligned with regional GTM, account priorities, and growth objectives</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build integrated field marketing plans that increase DAM awareness, engage buying groups, and convert priority accounts</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Pipeline Generation</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver qualified DAM pipeline targets alongside regional sales leadership, business development, and the DAM team</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Use account, intent, and market data to identify high-potential audiences, industries, and buying signals across EMEA</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Field Marketing Programs</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and deliver high-impact regional programs aligned with sales priorities, target account needs, and local market opportunities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create connected journeys across events, digital activation, executive engagement, and sales follow-up to move accounts through the funnel</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Campaign Execution</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Localize and activate global DAM campaigns, adapting the value proposition, messaging, content, and tactics for EMEA audiences</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own the execution of field events, webinars, executive programs, and digital campaigns that support Net New DAM acquisition</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Performance &amp; Optimization</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track and report campaign engagement, sourced and influenced pipeline, conversion, and ROI using agreed dashboards and reporting frameworks</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Continuously optimize audience, channel, content, and investment decisions based on performance data and stakeholder feedback</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration &amp; Enablement</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the DAM team, Corporate Marketing, Product Marketing, Regional Sales, Business Development, and Sales Enablement to align plans and resources</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted marketing advisor to sales teams, equipping them with DAM messaging, campaign plays, and timely follow-up guidance</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You Need to Succeed:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A minimum of 5 years of B2B marketing experience, ideally in SaaS, enterprise software, digital experience, content operations, or DAM</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven success in field marketing with responsibility for Net New pipeline creation across multiple EMEA markets</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of account-based marketing, buying groups, intent data, demand generation, and funnel acceleration</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience designing and executing integrated field programs that engage target accounts and accelerate pipeline; DAM or content technology experience is advantageous</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication, program management, and stakeholder management skills across regional and global teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proficiency in marketing automation, CRM, account intelligence, and analytics platforms</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent in English; additional European languages and experience marketing across diverse EMEA markets are a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Equal Opportunities at Sitecore</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sitecore is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace. We are committed to equal employment opportunity without unlawful regard to race, colour, ancestry, religion, gender, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital status, disability, veteran status or any other local legally protected characteristic.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/sitecore/field-marketing-manager-net-new-emea-dam-london-109374","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793050820},{"slug":"senior-strategic-partner-manager-london-207273","company_name":"Moss","title":"(Senior) Strategic Partner Manager   (f/m/d)","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At Moss, we give finance professionals the power to automate their day-to-day and make forward-thinking decisions.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our culture is what makes that possible: we play to win, we obsess over quality, and we win as One Moss, and it works. Moss closed a €35 million Series C in August 2026, crossing a €1 billion valuation, and became one of Europe's fintech unicorns. Join us for what's next.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>London, UK</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moss is building its strategic partnerships function from scratch, and this is one of the first two hires shaping it. You'll take target platforms from zero relationship to live, revenue-generating integration, owning the sourcing, business case, and delivery for each one.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a build phase: you'll define your own playbook rather than follow one. You'll report to the Senior Director Partnerships and work closely with Product and Engineering on integration scope, and with the Channel team where partnerships overlap with existing ERP integrators.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Source and build strategic partnerships from scratch, identifying platforms that fit Moss's customer base and growth priorities</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Navigate complex partner organisations to reach the right decision makers, from founders and C-level contacts at smaller platforms to Heads of Partnerships at larger ones</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build the commercial and technical case for each partnership and secure buy-in from both Moss leadership and the partner's stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own each partnership end-to-end, from an initial referral or lightweight integration through to a live, revenue-generating relationship</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product and Engineering to scope integration requirements and manage delivery against Moss's API and roadmap</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate with the Channel team where accounting-platform integrators already exist, to avoid overlap and align on commercialisation</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and adjust your own playbook, prioritising partners by revenue potential and strategic fit as the market picture sharpens</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About you</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">5+ years in business development or partnerships within B2B SaaS, fintech, cloud, or payments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">At least 2 years specifically in strategic partnerships or integration-led partner roles, having built relationships from scratch rather than managed an existing book</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of APIs and how software platforms integrate with external partner systems</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">In addition, here are the skills and attributes we are looking for:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Thrives with full ownership of a plan and pipeline, without needing day-to-day direction</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Brings structure to ambiguous, still-being-built processes and partnerships</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Communicates progress, blockers, and trade-offs clearly across product, engineering, and leadership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balances ambition with realism, adjusting timelines to partner readiness and internal constraints without losing momentum</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About Moss</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Moss is the Finance AI platform for Europe's mid-sized businesses, giving companies real-time visibility and full control over their spend. By automating card issuing, invoice management and expenses, Moss simplifies financial workflows and frees finance and accounting teams from manual, administrative work.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded in Berlin and used by more than 10,000 businesses including Flink, Schufa, n8n and Auto1, Moss has raised €220+ million to date and operates in Germany, the Netherlands, the UK and further EU markets. In August 2026, <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.getmoss.com/magazine/moss-series-c?origin-page=en-us%2Fcareers"><u>Moss closed a €35 million Series C </u></a>led by Portage, crossing a €1 billion valuation and becoming one of Europe's newest fintech unicorns. Moss is backed by investors including Valar Ventures, Tiger Global, Global Founders Capital, Cherry Ventures, A-Star.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're a team of 300+ people from 50+ nationalities across 5 offices in Europe and we hire, reward, and grow people based on <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.linkedin.com/company/moss-finance/life/c2ac8184-5388-4962-ad07-e0bcbfe080f0/?viewAsMember=true"><u>Moss DNA</u></a>: playing to win, obsessing over quality, winning as One Moss. If that's how you want to work, we want to hear from you. - here's <strong>what else to expect:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Top-of-market compensation package, including equity. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our vibrant offices are at the heart of our culture, where in-person time fuels collaboration and connection over weekly breakfasts and Friday demos.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional benefits include: 20 days “work from abroad”, 600EUR/GBP Learning &amp; Development Budget, and other local benefits.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Unless stated otherwise, benefits apply to full-time positions (interns and working students receive a tailored package).</em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>By applying for the above position, you will confirm that you have reviewed and agreed to our </strong></em><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.getmoss.com/privacy-policy"><em><strong><u>Data Privacy Policy</u></strong></em></a><em><strong>.</strong></em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/moss/senior-strategic-partner-manager-london-207273","tags":["Commercial"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793050818},{"slug":"data-privacy-analyst-regulatory-compliance-london-331652","company_name":"iwoca","title":"Data Privacy Analyst - Regulatory Compliance","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The company</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Small businesses move fast. Opportunities often don’t wait, and cash flow pressures can appear overnight. To keep going, and growing, SMEs need finance that’s as flexible and responsive as they are.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That's why we built iwoca. Our smart technology, data science and five-star customer service ensures business owners can act with the speed, confidence and control they need, exactly when it's needed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve already cleared the way for 100,000 businesses with more than £4 billion in funding. Our passionate team is driven to help even more SMEs succeed, through access to better finance and other services that make running a business easier. Our ultimate mission is to support one million SMEs in their defining moments, creating lasting impact for the communities and economies they drive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Compliance team’s mission is to keep iwoca a safe and trusted lender for UK small businesses, and to make the compliant path the easy path for the teams we work with.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We make sure iwoca meets its regulatory obligations, particularly the financial crime, sanctions and data protection requirements that apply across our suite of products and services.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are the second line of defence for the UK business. We advise the people building and running the business on what the rules require, set the policies and standards they work to, and test whether what happens in practice matches them. We work alongside the product teams so that each product meets its obligations and can grow.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data protection is central to what we do. We hold the data privacy function for the UK business and own how iwoca handles personal data end to end: the lawful basis for how customer, applicant and third-party data is used; data subject access requests and other individual rights; personal data breaches; retention and deletion; records of processing; marketing and consent; the privacy review of new products and features; and the governance of automated decisioning and AI tooling.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>How we work:</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We enable rather than block. The answer is rarely just “no” — it’s what it would take to get to yes, and what the firm is accepting if it goes ahead anyway.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We go to the source. Positions are grounded in the actual rule, regulation or guidance, and we can show where they come from.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re proportionate. Controls match the risk in front of us. We don’t build process for its own sake.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re close to the business. We work directly with Tech, Data, Credit, Operations and Legal, and we want to be in the room early rather than at the end.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Data Privacy Analyst you will run iwoca’s day-to-day UK data protection work and help the business apply UK GDPR, the Data Protection Act 2018 and PECR in practice. Your primary focus will be the statutory core: data subject access requests, data protection impact assessments, legitimate interests assessments, personal data breaches and records of processing.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The role is not only to run that work but to improve it. A significant part of the job is identifying where our privacy operations could be automated, supported by AI or otherwise improved, assessing what each option would take and what it would mean for compliance, and specifying it well enough for our Tech and Data teams to deliver.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">There is real room for the role to grow: as you build credibility, so does the scope, towards owning areas of the framework outright, leading on AI and automation governance, and taking a larger advisory remit across the business.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You will report to the Data Privacy Manager and work closely with the Head of Compliance who also acts as iwoca’s DPO, so you will have experienced support on the harder judgement calls. This is a hands-on role and the work is visible — much of it goes to senior stakeholders or to the regulator.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Impact and influence</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Individual rights and data breaches. Own data subject access requests from intake to response — scoping the search, applying exemptions and meeting the statutory deadline — along with erasure, rectification and objection requests. Triage and investigate suspected personal data breaches, assess them against the 72-hour notification test, and keep the breach register accurate.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Privacy assessments and advice. Assist with DPIAs, legitimate interests assessments and other privacy reviews on new products, features, suppliers and data flows. Be an accessible first point of contact for teams across iwoca with a data protection question, and give them an answer they can act on, early enough to shape what they build.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Records, policies and reporting. Keep the record of processing activities accurate as the business changes, hold the retention and deletion schedules to account, review data processing agreements with suppliers, help maintain our data protection policies and standards, and produce the privacy reporting that goes to senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI and automated decisioning. Help assess AI tooling and automated decision-making across lending and operations: what personal data goes in, what lawful basis supports it, what the model does with it, and what rights customers have over the outcome. That includes the risks specific to these systems — decisions taken without meaningful human involvement, bias in outcomes, unreliable model output — and recommending how we address them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Automation and improvement. Identify the manual steps in our privacy operations that should not be manual, assess the options, and set out the requirements and compliance implications clearly enough for Tech and Data to deliver them.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The requirements</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Essential skills</strong></em></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience. Experience in data protection or privacy operations, or in a compliance, legal, risk or operational role where data protection was a real part of the job.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Data protection knowledge. A solid practical understanding of UK GDPR, the Data Protection Act 2018 and PECR, and of how the ICO expects firms to apply them. Familiarity with the changes made by the Data (Use and Access) Act 2025 is an advantage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Privacy operations and assessments. Hands-on experience of statutory work: DSARs, DPIAs, legitimate interests assessments, breach handling, ROPA maintenance or data processing agreement review. You may not have done all of these — but we want to see that you have done some of them properly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI and automation. A real interest in, and working understanding of, how data protection law applies to AI and automated decision-making. Enough technical fluency to see where a manual process could be automated, set out what is needed, and hold your own in a conversation with engineers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stakeholder management: Comfortable dealing directly with product, engineering, marketing, credit and operations teams, and able to give a non-specialist a clear answer they can act on rather than a legal summary.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sector experience. Financial services or fintech, ideally in lending or payments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Credentials. A privacy or AI qualification such as CIPP/E, CIPM, or ICO-recognised practitioner certificates — or working towards one.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Practical tooling. Experience using Claude Code, LLMs or privacy management platforms.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The culture</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At iwoca, we prioritise a culture of learning, growth, and support, and invest in the development of our team members. We value thought and skill diversity, and encourage people to explore new areas of interest, adopt better tools – including AI – and apply sound judgement so our products and decisions improve over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The offices</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We put a lot of effort into making iwoca a great place to work:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices in London, Leeds, Berlin, and Frankfurt with plenty of drinks and snacks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events and community-led groups, including running groups, padel, and monthly ping-pong and pool competitions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical insurance from Vitality, including discounted gym membership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A choice between a dedicated dental plan or a health cash plan that reimburses everyday medical expenses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A private GP service (separate from Vitality) for you, your partner, and your dependents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days’ holiday per year, an extra day off for your birthday, the option to buy or sell an additional five days of annual leave, and unlimited unpaid leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A one-month, fully paid sabbatical after four years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instant access to external counselling and therapy sessions for team members that need emotional or mental health support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3% Pension contributions on total earnings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An employee equity incentive scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous parental leave and a nursery tax benefit scheme to help you save money.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electric car scheme and cycle to work scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two company retreats a year: we’ve been to France, Italy, Spain, and further afield.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">And to make sure we all keep learning, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A learning and development budget for everyone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company-wide talks with internal and external speakers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to learning platforms like Treehouse.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Useful links:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://coda.io/@iwocauk/iwoca-benefits-policies-uk"><u>iwoca benefits &amp; policies</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://coda.io/@iwocauk/interview-welcome-pack-tap"><u>Interview welcome pack</u></a></p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/iwoca/data-privacy-analyst-regulatory-compliance-london-331652","tags":["Finance","Legal and Compliance"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"London","created_at":1793050814},{"slug":"uk-communications-executive-london-77864","company_name":"iwoca","title":"UK Communications Executive","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The company</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Small businesses move fast. Opportunities often don’t wait, and cash flow pressures can appear overnight. To keep going, and growing, SMEs need finance that’s as flexible and responsive as they are.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">That's why we built iwoca. Our smart technology, data science and five-star customer service ensures business owners can act with the speed, confidence and control they need, exactly when it's needed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’ve already cleared the way for 100,000 businesses with more than £4 billion in funding. Our passionate team is driven to help even more SMEs succeed, through access to better finance and other services that make running a business easier. Our ultimate mission is to support one million SMEs in their defining moments, creating lasting impact for the communities and economies they drive.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is an opportunity to build your career in communications at a fast-growing fintech that's reshaping SME finance. You'll be part of iwoca's external communications team, helping drive coverage across our expanding product portfolio, working on data-led campaigns and supporting our work with government and policymakers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our comms function works across the business to position iwoca as a leading voice in SME finance. You'll collaborate closely with Product, Commercial, and Executive teams to translate business priorities into compelling narratives that drive both brand awareness and customer acquisition.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're looking for a Communications Executive with up to two years' experience to join our UK comms team. Working alongside the team, you'll help publish our major data-driven campaigns, own the communications for a couple of our newest products, and support our public affairs and policy work. You'll also help with the BAU media activities that keep iwoca front-of-mind with key journalists and stakeholders.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Examples of the type of work you'll be doing:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>1. Support data-driven PR campaigns</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working with the team, you'll run several established data-driven campaigns:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Top 25 UK Cities for SME Jobs:</strong> Our <a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.iwoca.co.uk/news/newcastle-named-top-british-city-to-work-for-an-sme"><u>annual ranking</u></a> combines ONS employment data, business figures, and economic indicators. You can refine the methodology if needed, analyse the latest data, and craft narratives for regional and national media.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>SME survey research:</strong> Twice a year you'll help commission original survey research, working with established research partners to design questionnaires capturing timely SME sentiment. You'll help ensure we generate "business news" coverage that responds to real economic issues.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be comfortable working with raw datasets - not just presenting finished analysis. Spotting surprising findings, identifying regional variations, understanding which angles interest journalists versus policymakers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>2. Start shouting about our new products</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll eventually own the communications for a couple of iwoca's newest products, working directly with Venture Leads to drive awareness and customer acquisition. Here are a few we've just launched that you could be working on:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Credit Compass:</em> Our credit-building tool helping SMEs improve their scores. You'll identify customer success stories, translate credit score trends into compelling narratives, and position this as iwoca's answer to the credit access gap.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>SME Insurance:</em> Help launch this proposition to market - identifying angles around why SMEs need this product and announce new strategic partners as and when we secure them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>iwoca Credit Card:</em> You'll be involved from the ground up - understanding competitive positioning, identifying what's newsworthy in a crowded market, building a launch campaign that breaks through.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>iwocaPay</em> (launched in 2020): Our instant payment solution - you'll help scale awareness as this product continues to grow, finding ongoing news hooks beyond what we've already done in recent years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">For each product, you'll get under the hood with the Venture Leads - understanding commercial objectives, customer pain points, competitive landscape - then translating that into comms plans that drive both coverage and business outcomes. You'll own two products, with the split decided once you're in the job.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>3. Support our public affairs and policy work</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">iwoca works with government and policymakers to make the case for better access to finance for small businesses. You'll support this work, engaging with relevant government departments, industry bodies and ministers where relevant. This could include:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tracking policy and regulatory developments that affect SMEs and SME lending.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Helping draft consultation responses, policy briefings and position papers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Using our lending and survey data to build the evidence behind our policy positions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Preparing briefing materials for meetings with officials, industry bodies and ministers.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The requirements</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Up to two years' experience in communications, PR, public affairs, policy, journalism or a related field. Internships and placements count, and we welcome recent graduates.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent writing skills with the ability to craft data-driven stories, press releases, briefing materials, and media pitches that cut through.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ability to work at pace across multiple projects simultaneously, with strong organisational skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll need to be confident managing and analysing data with either Excel or Google Sheets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A genuine interest in the economy, policy and politics, and how they affect small businesses.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bonus:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some experience in, or a strong interest in, tech, fintech, financial services or B2B technology.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience in public affairs, policy or government relations, or an understanding of how policy is made.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Any exposure to product launches or translating complex propositions into accessible narratives.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience pitching to journalists or securing coverage in relevant press.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working with senior stakeholders.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial awareness and understanding of what drives media coverage in fintech and SME finance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Familiarity with media monitoring tools (e.g., Signal AI, Cision) and ability to analyse coverage data to inform strategy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The culture</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At iwoca, we prioritise a culture of learning, growth, and support, and invest in the development of our team members. We value thought and skill diversity, and encourage people to explore new areas of interest, adopt better tools – including AI – and apply sound judgement so our products and decisions improve over time.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The offices</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We put a lot of effort into making iwoca a great place to work:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offices in London, Leeds, Berlin, and Frankfurt with plenty of drinks and snacks.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events and community-led groups, including running groups, padel, and monthly ping-pong and pool competitions.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The benefits</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Medical insurance from Vitality, including discounted gym membership.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A choice between a dedicated dental plan or a health cash plan that reimburses everyday medical expenses.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A private GP service (separate from Vitality) for you, your partner, and your dependents.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">25 days’ holiday per year, an extra day off for your birthday, the option to buy or sell an additional five days of annual leave, and unlimited unpaid leave.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A one-month, fully paid sabbatical after four years.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instant access to external counselling and therapy sessions for team members that need emotional or mental health support.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3% Pension contributions on total earnings.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">An employee equity incentive scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Generous parental leave and a nursery tax benefit scheme to help you save money.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Electric car scheme and cycle to work scheme.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Two company retreats a year: we’ve been to France, Italy, Spain, and further afield.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">And to make sure we all keep learning, we offer:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A learning and development budget for everyone.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Company-wide talks with internal and external speakers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to learning platforms like Treehouse.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Useful links:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://coda.io/@iwocauk/iwoca-benefits-policies-uk"><u>iwoca benefits &amp; policies</u></a></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://coda.io/@iwocauk/interview-welcome-pack-tap"><u>Interview welcome pack</u></a></p></li></ul><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk