don","created_at":1793029215},{"slug":"credit-control-and-billing-assistant-6-month-ftc-brighton-hove-96166","company_name":"Tillo","title":"Credit Control and Billing Assistant (6-month FTC)","description":"<ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we’re looking for: </strong>We are looking for someone <strong>motivated</strong> and energetic to join our growing Finance team. You'll need to be an excellent <strong>communicator</strong> as this role will see you supporting the team, the wider business and of course our customers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The challenge:</strong> Our Finance team pride themselves on <strong>excellence</strong> as a team as well as providing the best service to customers, suppliers &amp; other teams at Tillo.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Where you’ll work: </strong>This role will be based in our Hove office 2 days a week</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><a target="_blank" rel="noopener" href="https://www.tillo.io/the-tillo-difference"><strong>The Tillo Difference</strong></a></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're in the business of rewards and incentives, so we know a thing or two about the importance of giving back. We can't grow as a business without growing as individuals, so we are committed to providing a workplace where passionate, driven individuals can thrive. We value collaboration, trust, positivity, and a willingness to learn - only by working as a team will we reach our goals.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re the market leader in the UK and are active in a number of other markets including USA, Europe, Australia and India. 🌎</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1><strong>Job Summary:</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Credit Control and Billing Assistant will be part of a high-performing Finance Operations Team, delivering outstanding service to customers, suppliers, and business stakeholders, while supporting the development and maintenance of best-in-class operational processes and controls.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tillo is a fast-growing, private equity–backed, international FinTech business. This role plays a key part in managing accounts receivable ledgers, collections, delivering process improvements and automation, and providing support with weekly and monthly reconciliations</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>Day to day this role will</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively manage credit control and collections activities, following up on overdue balances and resolving customer queries.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Ensure accurate and timely invoicing, maintaining the integrity of the billing cycle end to end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Investigate and respond to invoicing queries from customers and internal stakeholders in a timely and professional manner.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with the Operations team to deliver an effective onboarding experience for new retailers, suppliers, and customers.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with Account Management and Commercial teams to minimise overdue balances</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborating proactively with the wider finance team to support with the implementation of billing and credit control process improvement initiatives and uphold best practices for a robust Credit Control and Billing function.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h2><strong>What we’re looking for</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Essential:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven experience in credit control and billing, including managing collections, resolving invoicing queries, and maintaining accurate accounts receivable records.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven ability to build and manage effective supplier and stakeholder relationships.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Innovative problem-solver with exceptional attention to detail and a proactive, solution-oriented mindset.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong communicator and organizer, capable of liaising effectively with internal teams and external partners to achieve objectives.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Desirable:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demonstrated track record of continuous process improvement, driving efficiency, accuracy, and scalability.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience within a fintech, high growth or dynamic environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A keen interest in working with AI tools</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><h1>Benefits</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">We offer all our employees trust and empower our team to work with flexibility and autonomy. We’re a close-knit team and love working collaboratively, with our hybrid model, our team can come together at our fantastic office in Hove, but also focus in their own space. The Tillo team are a motivated bunch and we all work hard to push Tillo forwards, always innovating. We completely understand the importance of work/life balance and offer a supportive and collaborative working environment with the following benefits:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Enhanced annual leave of 26 days per annum (plus an additional day for your birthday 🎂)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Private Medical care through Vitality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Employee Incentive Scheme</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to Tillo’s Storefront with discounts &amp; gift card vouchers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hybrid Working</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Top spec equipment including laptop, mouse, keyboard, monitor</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Anniversary gifts</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Monthly breakfasts, drinks, snacks and events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team Learning &amp; Development budget</p></li></ul><h2><strong>About Tillo</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tillo makes gift cards, rewards, and incentives simple, efficient, and profitable. Operating in over 37 markets and 25 currencies, Tillo processes billions in gift card transactions through a single, plug-and-go API, powering rewards and incentives for the world’s leading businesses.<br /><br />Backed by Tenzing, Tillo is setting the global standard for digital gift card infrastructure.<br /><br /><strong>Diversity, Equity, and Inclusion Statement<br /></strong><em>We are committed to fostering a diverse and inclusive workplace where everyone feels valued and respected.  We welcome applications from individuals of all backgrounds, regardless of age, disability, gender identity, marital status, race, ethnicity, religion or belief, sex, or sexual orientation. <br /><br />If you require any reasonable adjustments during the recruitment process, please let us know, and we will be happy to accommodate your needs.</em></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/tillo/credit-control-and-billing-assistant-6-month-ftc-brighton-hove-96166","tags":["Finance"],"job_types":["Contract"],"location":"Hove Office","created_at":1793029212},{"slug":"engineering-intern-london-summer-2027-229299","company_name":"Hiya","title":"Engineering Intern (London, Summer 2027)","description":"<h2><strong>About Hiya</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Hiya, we’re making business calls more trusted, useful, and effective.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Voice remains one of the most important ways businesses communicate with their customers, but the value of a call depends on trust. When customers do not recognize who is calling or why, important conversations are missed, customer relationships suffer, and business outcomes are harder to achieve.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiya helps businesses create trusted calling experiences that benefit both sides of the conversation: enterprises can reach customers with confidence, and customers can answer with confidence. Our products support branded business calling, trusted caller identity, call performance insights, customer engagement, and voice security capabilities that help businesses strengthen relationships and improve outcomes.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role sits in a core business area for Hiya and is focused on helping SMB and enterprise customers succeed.</p><h2><strong>About the Role</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">The engineering intern position is for an individual contributor who is responsible for architecting, implementing, and maintaining significant systems that serve hundreds of millions of requests per month. Hiya provides high-availability, latency-sensitive capabilities to telecoms, mobile apps, and other partners. In addition, you'll work with engineering teams across Hiya, some in Seattle and some in Europe, to define and deliver shared components and services. From day one, you will be paired with a dedicated mentor who provides structured guidance, technical feedback, and ongoing career mentorship.</p><h2><strong>What You'll Do</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design, code, and operate high-performance services and data processing pipelines on a modern technology stack, supported by a structured technical crash course during your first two weeks covering our core tools, architecture, and repositories.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work at a supportive and fast-growing startup with a fantastic team, where you can collaborate with and learn from other great team members.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Make an impact in the lives of hundreds of millions of consumers.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Be supported in developing your skills and accelerating your career.</p><h2><strong>What We Are Looking For</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Engineering:</strong> CS majors - 2nd year (graduating 2028) </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excitement to work on  innovative technology advancements</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A philosophy of iteration and continuous improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of building services that adhere to operational SLAs</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A preference for velocity over perfection</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A commitment to respectful and impactful collaboration</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Self-motivated and excited to learn about new technologies</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Our Interview Process: The Hiya Voice AI Challenge</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Once we’ve confirmed your eligibility, you’ll receive the Hiya Voice AI Challenge by email-- a chance to build a working prototype of a voice-driven product in one of five tracks: Accessibility, Productivity, Creative Voice, Security, or Real-Time Assistance. You’ll have one week to build it, with optional virtual office hours along the way if you’d like to pitch your idea and get steering from our team first.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From there:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Submit and get reviewed.</strong> One of our engineers reviews your work. If we’d like to explore your project further, you’ll get a link to book a 30-minute virtual session with an engineer or two-- a quick demo, a walkthrough of your code, and some questions.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Final interviews, in person at Hiya.</strong> Candidates who advance join us for a final round in London (<strong>2nd &amp; 3rd of December)</strong>: a debugging/fixing session, a chance to add a feature to your own project, and a conversation about Hiya’s values.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI tools are welcome and encouraged the whole way through.</p><h2><strong>What You Can Expect From Us</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Dedicated technical mentorship with structured, regular feedback check-ins</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Clear project scope and goals provided right at the start of your internship</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comprehensive onboarding to get you up to speed on Hiya's tooling, codebases, and systems quickly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A supportive, collaborative environment built on psychological safety and genuine impact</p></li></ul><h2><strong>How We Work</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hiya is not a passive environment. We expect people to take ownership, form opinions, and engage directly with hard problems.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We work with a high degree of <strong>transparency and autonomy</strong>. Context is shared openly, and decisions are discussed, challenged, and then made. Once a call is made, we commit and move forward.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll be expected to work through ambiguity, weigh tradeoffs, and take responsibility for results, while keeping a high bar for quality and customer trust.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Every team member at Hiya is expected to live our core values:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Serve, our customers and partners by holding a high bar for trust and quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own, share in success and open up to failures</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead, listen, show up with a point of view but commit entirely once a decision has been made</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Improve, even if it means changing course or contradicting ourselves</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Do, rather than observe</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Come Work With Us!</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building a team with diverse perspectives, identities, and professional experiences. We evaluate candidates through a business lens and believe that diversity and unique viewpoints make our company stronger, more dynamic, and a great place to build a career.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We've been recognized by Built In, GeekWire, Comparably, G2, Forbes, and Deloitte Technology Fast 500 for our culture, innovation, leadership, compensation, and more. At Hiya, we're a people-centric company focused on helping each employee grow both personally and professionally. We create a culture of support and empowerment that challenges the status quo, resulting in an energized team that's passionate about their work. You'll love working here if you're looking for an innovative challenge that's disrupting an industry. Come join us!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em>Hiya is an equal opportunity employer. We celebrate diversity and are committed to building an inclusive environment for all employees.</em></p><hr><p>Compensation: £45K</p><ul><li> • £45,000 Annual-equivalent, pro-rated across 12 weeks, plus pension £45K</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/hiya/engineering-intern-london-summer-2027-229299","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Intern"],"location":"London, UK","created_at":1793029212},{"slug":"account-executive-high-growth-french-speaking-london-greater-london-269644","company_name":"Alphasense","title":"Account Executive, High Growth (French Speaking)","description":"&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&q