&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;Liftoff offers a fast-paced, collaborative, and innovative work environment where employees are empowered to grow and make an impact. We’re shaping the future of the mobile app ecosystem—join us and help accelerate what’s next.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff’s compensation strategy includes competitive salaries, equity, and benefits designed to support employee well-being and performance. We benchmark compensation based on role, level, and location to ensure fairness and market alignment. Benefits may include medical coverage, wellness stipends, and additional perks based on your country of residence.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Liftoff is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to creating an inclusive environment for all employees and applicants regardless of race, ethnicity, national origin, age, marital status, disability, sexual orientation, gender identity, religion, veteran status, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Agency and Third Party Recruiter Notice:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Liftoff does not accept unsolicited resumes from individual recruiters or third-party recruiting agencies in response to job postings. No fee will be paid to third parties who submit unsolicited candidates directly to our hiring managers or Recruiting Team. All candidates must be submitted via our Applicant Tracking System by approved Liftoff vendors who have been expressly requested to make a submission by our Recruiting Team for a specific job opening. No placement fees will be paid to any firm unless such a request has been made by the Liftoff Recruiting Team and such a candidate was submitted to the Liftoff Recruiting Team via our Applicant Tracking System.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/liftoff/commercial-legal-counsel-contractor-364228","tags":["Exec & Legal"],"job_types":[],"location":"","created_at":1793008520},{"slug":"junior-marketing-manager-london-44573","company_name":"Mammutmarsch UG","title":"Junior Marketing Manager (m/f/d)","description":"<h2>About us</h2><p>Mammutmarsch is adventure at heart - and pushing limits in practice. We’re the movement behind long-distance hiking events that inspire people to grow beyond themselves. Now we’re taking the next step: preparing our market entry in the UK - and we’re looking for a freelance Marketing Manager to help make it happen.</p><h2>Your Impact</h2><p>Together with our marketing team, you’ll launch Mammutmarsch in the UK - from local marketing ideas to first campaigns and partnerships. You’ll bring your market understanding, execute independently, and turn concepts into real resonance within the community.</p><h2><strong>How we work</strong></h2><p>Remote‑first, pragmatic, and hands‑on. We decide close to the goal, test fast, learn faster, and deliver bold ideas - with team spirit, creativity, clear communication, and ownership.</p><h2><strong>Your responsibilities</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Go-to-market UK: develop local marketing plans, roadmap, and launch initial activities</p></li><li><p>Social media first: plan, create, and publish UK-adapted content; own the editorial calendar and posting cadence</p></li><li><p>Community building: engage in dialogue, handle comments/DMs, uphold community guidelines, and systematically grow organic reach</p></li><li><p>Campaign execution: run and continuously optimize social and influencer campaigns</p></li><li><p>Content production: create short clips/UGC, snippets, visuals, and copy tailored to the UK</p></li><li><p>Performance basics: track KPIs, deliver reports, and translate insights into action</p></li><li><p>Secondary: research relevant partners/networks and initiate selectively when useful</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you bring</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Initial professional experience in marketing (e.g., social, influencer, PR, campaigns, community)</p></li><li><p>Highly self‑driven, solutions‑oriented working style and a passion for building new structures</p></li><li><p>Creativity and the courage to take new paths</p></li><li><p>Excellent UK market understanding: culture, trends, media / platforms; sharp language instincts</p></li><li><p>Language skills: English at native or near‑native level; additional languages are a plus</p></li><li><p>Willingness to travel for occasional UK activities</p></li><li><p>Enthusiasm for our mission and events</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Our promise</strong></h2><ul><li><p>Direct collaboration with our core marketing team</p></li><li><p>Plenty of creative freedom, responsibility, and fast impact</p></li><li><p>Flexible, fully remote collaboration (freelance, 15–20 hrs/week)</p></li><li><p>Fair compensation, clear goals, and short decision paths</p></li><li><p>The chance to help build Mammutmarsch in the UK from day one</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Your application</strong></h2><p>Sound like you? Apply with the button on this page and send us your CV / portfolio, your hourly rate and 2–3 short samples of your work (e.g., posts, campaigns, a mini case), plus a few lines on why the UK is your playground. We usually get back within four working days.</p><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/jobs/companies/mammutmarsch-ug/junior-marketing-manager-london-44573","tags":["Remote","Marketing Manager"],"job_types":["Self-employed contractor (freelancer)","freelance","entry"],"location":"London","created_at":1793007048},{"slug":"remote-analyst-investor-relations-marketing-france-365338","company_name":"Re7 Capital","title":"Analyst, Investor Relations & Marketing","description":"<p>Remote-First | Working hours: UK or CET time zone | Full-time</p><h3>The role</h3><p>Reporting directly to the Head of Investor Relations, you will support how Re7 is positioned with institutional allocators and the wider market. This includes helping to prepare and maintain investor materials and marketing content, and contributing to the firm’s media presence. The role offers broad exposure to investor relations and marketing at an institutional DeFi investment firm.</p><h3>What you'll do</h3><p><strong>BD &amp; IR Support</strong></p><ul><li>Build and maintain targeted investor and partner lists for outreach</li><li>Keep the CRM and the data room up to date</li><li>Maintain fund performance, AUM and factsheets across hedge fund databases</li><li>Support preparation of DDQs, and maintain a library of standard responses</li></ul><p><strong>Marketing &amp; PR</strong></p><ul><li>Build and maintain relationships with crypto, financial and fund industry media for Re7 Capital and Re7 Labs</li><li>Track speaking opportunities, podcasts and award submissions on a rolling calendar</li><li>Log media coverage and appearances, and keep the website up to date</li><li>Contribute ideas to campaign and content planning</li><li>Schedule social media posts and track performance across X, LinkedIn and Telegram</li><li>Create branded visuals in Canva and lay out research papers and marketing materials</li><li>Support the production of newsletters, press releases and other written content</li><li>Shortlist venues, request quotes and coordinate logistics and branding for events</li></ul><p><strong>Requirements</strong></p><ul><li>At least 1 year of experience in a finance-related role (e.g. investment management, real estate, private markets, fintech or crypto)</li><li>A genuine interest in DeFi and digital asset markets</li><li>Excellent written English</li><li>Highly organised, with strong attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple deadlines</li><li>Good working knowledge of Canva and Google Workspace</li><li>Hands-on experience using AI tools, including prompt design and building simple workflows or automations (e.g. with Claude or no-code tools)</li><li>Able to work closely to a brief and handle confidential information with discretion</li></ul><p><strong>Benefits</strong></p><p></p><ul><li>Remote-first structure with opportunities for in-person collaboration</li><li>Collaborative, high-performance culture</li><li>Exposure to cutting-edge crypto and digital asset strategies</li><li>Competitive compensation package</li></ul><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/re7-capital/remote-analyst-investor-relations-marketing-france-365338","tags":["Marketing","Information Technology and Services","Capital","Remote"],"job_types":["Full time","internship"],"location":"France","created_at":1793067611},{"slug":"ops-associate-paris-338075","company_name":"Parallel","title":"Ops Associate","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>At Parallel, we build AI agents to help healthcare facilities automate their administrative processes and unlock additional revenue, starting with medical coding.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br />Today, up to 25% of healthcare spending is lost in manual, repetitive administrative work. Legacy software hasn’t helped, it’s made things slower, more complex, and more frustrating for care teams.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe AI agents can change that. Our technology combines Large Language Models with system-level automation to handle real work inside existing hospital tools. No integrations, no disruption.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our first agent automates coding workflows and frees up time for medical staff to focus on patients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We launched in 2024, are backed by top investors (Index, Frst, Y Combinator, Hexa, Kima Ventures, Better Angle), and we’re just getting started.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">The future of healthcare isn’t just digital — it’s automated. Come help us build it !</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The role</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Parallel, we work with a team of 25+ freelance TIMs (medical information technicians) on different tasks, in particular retrieving medical documents from our partner facilities’ software. This is a core part of Parallel. With fast, secure access to our partner facilities’ data, we code the first hospital stays within a few days and prove Parallel’s ROI. Then we automate document extraction so we can scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As Ops Associate, you support the Ops team on managing freelancers and on cross-functional Ops projects. You take ownership of critical operational topics end to end and contribute directly to Parallel’s growth. You work daily with our Head of Ops, the Deployment Strategists, Customer Care and our freelance TIMs.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re in charge of staffing and managing our network of freelance TIMs and become their main point of contact, working directly with our Head of Ops. You also work on cross-functional projects that structure Ops as Parallel scales. It’s a chance to see first-hand how a generative AI solution is deployed in hospitals, and to experience a startup’s scale-up from the inside.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Staffing and management of freelance TIMs</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re responsible for the network of freelance TIMs who support our clients. You make sure the right person is on the right assignment, at the right time, within a compliant framework.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Sourcing and recruiting</strong>: identify, qualify and recruit new TIMs based on needs (specialties, facilities, volume).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Staffing assignments</strong>: assign TIMs to client accounts, anticipate workload peaks and manage priorities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Onboarding</strong>: train new TIMs on the Parallel tool and our ways of working.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Monitoring</strong>: centralize assignment tracking and manage the team’s performance.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Contracts and compliance</strong>: keep freelance contracts up to date, in line with our ISO 27001 and HDS requirements (data access, confidentiality).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Cross-functional Ops projects</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You support the Ops team on cross-functional projects to make processes more robust and scalable. For example, you could:</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compliance and security</strong>: contribute to the ISO 27001 and HDS certification project on the Ops side (registers, evidence, access reviews, contracts).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Processes and documentation</strong>: keep client training notes up to date and improve internal playbooks (deployment, support).</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who we’re looking for</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re looking for your first permanent job, or possibly an end-of-studies internship (with the goal of staying with us on a permanent contract).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re rigorous: you organize yourself, prioritize, and follow your topics through to the end.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You have strong people skills: you can adapt to profiles very different from yours, explain technical topics and bring a team along.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re comfortable in a tech environment and like understanding how software works so you can help others use it.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’re autonomous: when you’re given an assignment, you figure out how to set up the right processes and resources to get it done.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Why join us?</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Real impact</strong>: our agents free hospital teams from administrative work.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>A central role</strong>: you work with Ops, Product, Tech and the field teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Room to grow</strong>: we’re hiring for this role to help someone grow with us over time.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The right time</strong>: Series A closed, product already used by ~100 hospitals, a fast-growing team.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The package</strong>: Alan health insurance, Swile, Apple equipment, 50% of transport covered, a team event every month and two off-sites a year.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Our offices</strong>: Paris 2nd arrondissement, boulevard de Sébastopol.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>The process</strong></p><ol style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Call with Léa, Talent Lead (30 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Call with Clémentine, Head of Ops and your future manager (30 min)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Case study with Clémentine and Jules and meeting with Paul, CEO</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Offer</p></li></ol><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We care about who you are, not just what's on your CV.</strong><br /><br />If you're drawn to what we're building but don't meet every requirement, we still want to hear from you. Studies show that women in particular tend to apply only when they meet 100% of the criteria. If that's you, please don't let that hold you back. We'd love to receive your application.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.fr/jobs/companies/parallel/ops-associate-paris-338075","tags":["Operations & Account Management"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Paris","created_at":1793061613},{"slug":"intern-digital-art-director-paris-9th-arrondissement-of-paris-75009-paris-197693","company_name":"Artefactjobs","title":"Intern - Digital Art Director - Paris","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qui sommes-nous ?&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Artefact 3000 est la &lt;strong&gt;division Créative &amp;amp; Data&lt;/strong&gt; du groupe Artefact. Notre singularité réside dans notre capacité à marier l&#39;audace créative avec la rigueur de la &lt;strong&gt;science des données et de l&#39;Intelligence Artificielle&lt;/strong&gt;. Nous ne faisons pas que de la publicité ; nous concevons l&#39;esthétique et l&#39;exécution d&#39;&lt;strong&gt;expériences digitales et de campagnes data-driven&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nous sommes l&#39;agence de référence pour les marques qui cherchent à faire évoluer leur communication sur tous les supports numériques. Notre expertise couvre la conception visuelle de campagnes d&#39;envergure, d&#39;activations d&#39;&lt;strong&gt;IA générative&lt;/strong&gt;, de contenus sociaux impactants et de dispositifs &lt;strong&gt;web immersifs&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partenaire d&#39;innovation pour des clients majeurs tels que&lt;strong&gt; Groupe ADP, WWF, Robertet, Pierre&amp;amp;Vacances, TF1+, TotalEnergies&lt;/strong&gt;, nous avons reçu de nombreuses récompenses pour notre créativité et notre innovation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Les missions que nous proposons&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Au sein de l’agence, vous accompagnez les Directeurs Artistiques dans la mise en production des campagnes : votre rôle est de transformer les concepts en livrables impeccables, déclinés sur l&#39;ensemble des formats digitaux, avec un vrai souci du détail et du craft.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Décliner et produire les kits créatifs sur tous les formats : bannières display &lt;strong&gt;statiques et animées&lt;/strong&gt;, formats social, habillages web, en respectant les chartes et les intentions créatives.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Assurer l&#39;exécution graphique et le craft des livrables (typographie, couleur, composition, finition pixel perfect), dans une logique de qualité et de cohérence multi-formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Produire des contenus animés simples : déclinaisons motion de bannières et de stories à partir de maquettes et de storyboards existants.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Apporter votre regard et participer à la direction artistique de certains projets : recherche de références, planches d&#39;intentions, moodboards, propositions de key visuals.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Être force de proposition sur les outils de production, y compris l&#39;IA générative, pour gagner en efficacité et en qualité d&#39;exécution.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Le profil que nous recherchons&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Étudiant/étudiante en fin d&#39;études d&#39;une école de Design Graphique, de Création Publicitaire ou d&#39;Arts Appliqués, vous disposez idéalement d&#39;une première expérience en agence ou en studio sur des productions digitales.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Solide culture visuelle et graphique, sens du détail et réelle exigence sur le craft (typographie, couleur, composition, finition).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Goût pour la production et la déclinaison : vous aimez voir vos livrables aboutis et déployés proprement sur tous les formats.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise indispensable de la Suite Adobe (Photoshop, Illustrator) et de Figma.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maîtrise du Motion Design (Adobe After Effects) attendue, ou forte appétence pour l&#39;animation de bannières et de formats sociaux.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Curiosité pour les nouvelles technologies et les outils de création par IA générative (Midjourney, Higgsfield, Kling, etc.) : un vrai plus.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Rigueur, organisation et capacité à gérer plusieurs livrables en parallèle dans le respect des délais.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pourquoi nous rejoindre :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Artefact 3000 est l&#39;agence où il faut être : venez développer votre savoir-faire dans une agence de publicité technophile qui monte, qui monte…&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Progression : chaque jour offre de nouveaux défis et de nouvelles occasions d&#39;apprendre, sur des marques fortes et des projets variés.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Culture : rejoignez la meilleure équipe que vous puissiez imaginer.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Process de recrutement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;1er entretien : Farouk, Directeur Artistique&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;2e entretien : Clara, Talent Specialist Acquisition&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Come join us!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
