ent fine-tuning of large-scale models.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Algorithm Optimization:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Optimize model inference for real-time robotic applications without compromising reasoning capabilities.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Publication &amp; Visibility:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the global research community by publishing high-impact papers at top-tier conferences (NeurIPS, CVPR, ICRA, CoRL, etc.).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaboration:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work closely with the Core Robotics and Hardware teams to integrate AI models into our physical platforms.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Qualifications:</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Academic Excellence:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">PhD or Master’s degree in Computer Science, Machine Learning, Robotics, or a related field, with a focus on Deep Learning and Computer Vision.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven Research Track Record:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Significant publications and citations at major conferences such as NeurIPS, CVPR, ICCV, ICRA, IROS, or CoRL.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Professional Background:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working in leading AI research environments</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Technical Mastery:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep expertise in PyTorch or JAX, experience with Transformers, Diffusion Models, and Large Language Models (LLMs).</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Domain Knowledge:</strong> </p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong understanding of Vision-Language models and their application to Action/Control loops in robotics.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>Location:</strong></h1><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zurich Area, Switzerland: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in our Zurich office, offering a vibrant ecosystem for robotics and AI.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free meals at the workplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours and the option to work from home when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct collaboration with founders and world-leading AI experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to large-scale compute clusters and proprietary robotic datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A key role in shaping the future of embodied AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation and a relocation package for the Zurich area</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/sereact-gmbh/member-of-technical-staff-zurich-24981","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1792885215},{"slug":"research-engineer-zurich-318019","company_name":"Sereact GmbH","title":"Research Engineer (m/f/d)","description":"<h1>Research Engineer, Manipulation Data &amp; Teleoperation — Zurich</h1><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role owns the data generation layer of Sereact's VLA stack: teleoperation systems and data collection infrastructure that feed Cortex, built from our Zurich research hub.</p><h2>About Sereact</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sereact is a Series B embodied-AI company. Cortex, our VLA model, is deployed in live warehouse robotic cells across the EU and US. Zurich is our newest research hub, focused on the manipulation and control problems that sit underneath Cortex.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>The role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a Research Engineer position. It is scoped to the data generation layer of the VLA stack: teleoperation hardware and software, retargeting pipelines that map human demonstrations onto robot hands, and the data collection infrastructure that feeds Cortex. It requires building the systems that produce the data those models train on, and working closely with the training team on what that data needs to look like.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you'll do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build and operate teleoperation systems for dexterous manipulation, including retargeting algorithms that map human hand and arm motion onto robot end-effectors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Design and maintain scalable, UMI-style data collection hardware and software that other engineers at Sereact rely on</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Benchmark control and retargeting approaches using rigorous, human-factors-informed methodology</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Instrument and support the physical robots deployed in the Zurich hub, including day-to-day work on the control stack</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with the model-training team to define what data they need and close the loop on data quality</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build tooling or infrastructure outside your immediate brief when it unblocks the wider team</p></li></ul><h2>What you'll bring</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">MSc (or equivalent, in progress) in robotics, mechanical engineering, or a closely related field, with a thesis or capstone project on manipulation, teleoperation, or retargeting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Hands-on experience building a data collection device or system for robot learning (UMI or a comparable system), not just operating one someone else built</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Working knowledge of retargeting algorithms for mapping human input onto robot hands or end-effectors</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">1 to 2 years of combined research, internship, or industry experience in robotics, mechatronics, or a related engineering discipline</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Software and systems engineering skills strong enough to build and maintain infrastructure other engineers rely on, not only research-grade prototypes</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable working as an individual contributor in a small, still-forming team</p></li></ul><h2>Nice to have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A conference submission on manipulation, teleoperation, or retargeting where the candidate is an author (an MSc thesis submitted to a venue like CoRL counts; supervising a student team whose own work was later published does not)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Teaching or TA experience in a robotics course</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Some exposure to large-model training, even without an independent training record</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A concrete example of building something outside the formal role brief because the team needed it</p></li></ul><h2><strong>Location:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Zurich Area, Switzerland: </strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in our Zurich office, offering a vibrant ecosystem for robotics and AI.</p></li></ul><h1><strong>What We Offer:</strong></h1><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Free meals at the workplace.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Flexible working hours and the option to work from home when needed.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Direct collaboration with founders and world-leading AI experts.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Access to large-scale compute clusters and proprietary robotic datasets.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A key role in shaping the future of embodied AI.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive compensation and a relocation package for the Zurich area</p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.ch/jobs/companies/sereact-gmbh/research-engineer-zurich-318019","tags":["Software"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Zurich","created_at":1792885215},{"slug":"mission-critical-security-engineer-threat-hunting-schiphol-rijk-484413","company_name":"Schubergphilis","title":"Mission Critical Security Engineer – Threat Hunting","description":"&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Help protect what truly matters in our customers&#39; most critical environments by proactively identifying threats and improving how they are detected and addressed.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Mission Critical Security Engineer with a focus on Threat Hunting, you will be part of a dedicated customer team responsible for securing and continuously improving a complex, mission-critical application landscape.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Working alongside other engineers and security specialists, you will help ensure the environment remains as secure and resilient as possible. You combine a strong engineering foundation with a security mindset, taking ownership of security improvements and understanding how systems, applications, and infrastructure behave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Your specific focus will be on threat hunting and detection engineering. Using your in-depth knowledge of the customer&#39;s technology stack and application landscape, you will fine-tune existing detection use cases and develop new ones tailored to the environment. You will use our custom SIEM/SOAR-based Managed Detection and Response (MDR) platform to turn emerging threats and technical insights into actionable detection capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role bridges security engineering, detection engineering, and threat intelligence. You don&#39;t simply follow predefined playbooks. You understand system behavior, identify gaps, and develop practical solutions that strengthen the security of the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What you will do&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Threat intelligence &amp;amp; continuous improvement&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Actively follow security developments, vulnerabilities, and threat intelligence and translate these into relevant hunts and detections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Identify security risks and gaps in detection coverage and proactively propose improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use your knowledge of the customer&#39;s application and infrastructure landscape to continuously strengthen its security posture.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to the evolution of the team&#39;s security monitoring and detection strategy.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication &amp;amp; advisory&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate findings into clear, actionable communication for engineers, customer stakeholders, and security specialists.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Contribute to security advisories and share relevant threats across the customer team and wider organization.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Work closely with engineers to understand system behavior and validate detection strategies.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with the customer&#39;s Security Operations Center (SOC) to align security monitoring, threat detection, and response activities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Help establish and improve integrations with the customer&#39;s SIEM/SOAR platform, including the forwarding of relevant logs and security telemetry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Detection engineering &amp;amp; threat hunting&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Develop and continuously improve detection use cases based on emerging threats and observed behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Translate threat scenarios and security insights into actionable detection logic tailored to the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proactively perform threat hunting across the application and infrastructure landscape to identify abnormal or suspicious patterns.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Analyze logs and telemetry data to uncover behaviors that are not yet covered by existing detections.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Use your understanding of the customer&#39;s technology stack to distinguish normal from potentially malicious behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Use case development &amp;amp; response design&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define what should happen when detections trigger, including response actions, automation, and escalation paths.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Continuously refine detection logic to improve quality, relevance, and signal-to-noise ratio.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and fine-tune custom detection scenarios based on the specific characteristics and security requirements of the customer&#39;s environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Platform collaboration&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Leverage our custom SIEM/SOAR-based MDR platform to implement detections and analyze data.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with platform and automation engineers to improve integrations and detection capabilities.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Apply engineering and automation practices to ensure detection solutions are scalable, reliable, and maintainable.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What you bring&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for someone who combines solid engineering fundamentals with a strong interest in security and is motivated to move towards or deepen their expertise in threat hunting and detection engineering.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t necessarily need to be an experienced threat hunter already. What matters is your ability to understand complex systems, recognize unusual behavior, and translate technical insights into practical security improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Solid engineering fundamentals, including Linux, networking, and infrastructure behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with cloud environments such as AWS, Azure, or similar platforms.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with CI/CD, Git, and configuration management or infrastructure-as-code tooling.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong automation mindset and the ability to translate problems into scalable solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience working with logs and telemetry to analyze system behavior and investigate technical issues.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with Python and/or Bash scripting.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with SIEM or log analytics platforms such as OpenSearch, Elastic, Splunk, or Microsoft Sentinel.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong understanding of security principles, including threat detection and response.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to distinguish normal from abnormal system behavior.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Analytical, curious, and driven to understand how systems and threats behave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ownership mindset, with responsibility for security quality and continuous improvement.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Strong communication skills to translate technical findings into actionable insights.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ability to connect business and customer context to technical security solutions.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-have skills&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul data-spread=&quot;false&quot;&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Hands-on experience with threat hunting, detection engineering, or advanced SOC operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience developing or improving detection use cases and security monitoring rules.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience with SOAR or security automation.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep knowledge of Microsoft Entra ID, Azure, and other Microsoft cloud services.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Familiarity with threat intelligence frameworks such as MITRE ATT&amp;amp;CK.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Experience integrating SIEM/SOAR platforms or forwarding security telemetry between different environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ Who are you?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You are an engineer with a strong interest in security, driven to understand how systems behave and how threats manifest.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don&#39;t follow playbooks blindly. You want to understand why detections exist, how systems interact, and where security can be improved.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You combine analytical thinking with a hands-on mindset and enjoy working with complex applications, infrastructure, and data. You are curious, proactive, and take ownership of the quality of your work.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You also enjoy being part of a customer team where security is a shared responsibility. You work closely with fellow engineers and security specialists, communicate clearly with stakeholders, and contribute to keeping the entire environment secure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;/ What can you expect?&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At Schuberg Philis, you&#39;ll join a community of engineers with an awesome combination of exceptionally high security standards, an infatuation with automation, and the power to make a positive, sustainable impact on customers&#39; business.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work within a dedicated customer team where engineers and security specialists jointly take responsibility for the security and reliability of mission-critical environments.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Due to the nature of our customer engagements, there is no pressure on (billable) hours; we focus on quality and impact or how we like to call it:&amp;nbsp;&lt;strong&gt;freedom &amp;amp; responsibility&lt;/strong&gt;. You know best how to deliver the most value.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll be embedded in a company committed to helping colleagues grow as people and professionals through training, knowledge sharing, mentoring, and good old-fashioned fun.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Our offices are high-quality workspaces, and we go way beyond what is expected. We have productive equipment, good food and drinks, team outings, family days, labs to experiment with innovative technologies, etc.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We&#39;re active in relevant tech communities, attending and organizing meetups and conferences, and we organize internal knowledge-sharing events where Tech Leads play an important role.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you&#39;re an engineer in the Netherlands with a strong interest in security and want to help secure mission-critical environments while developing or deepening your expertise in threat hunting and detection engineering, we&#39;d love to hear from you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;div&gt;&lt;hr&gt;&lt;/div&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Everyone we work with and consider working with has a right to equal treatment. The hiring and appraisal process at Schuberg Philis is designed to be thorough and equitable, implementing fair payment, benefits, and opportunities across all demographics.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/em&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;em&gt;It is our desire to be a company that brings together multiple nationalities, cultures, religions, genders, abilities, and talents within and across our teams. We welcome colleagues from diverse backgrounds to join Schuberg Philis and actively support diversity and inclusion in the tech industry.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/schubergphilis/mission-critical-security-engineer-threat-hunting-schiphol-rijk-484413","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":[],"location":"Schiphol-Rijk","created_at":1793062522},{"slug":"junior-product-manager-it-fulfillment-amsterdam-209861","company_name":"Suitsupply","title":"Junior Product Manager – IT Fulfillment","description":"&lt;h6&gt;Every order a Suitsupply customer places, online, in a store, or through customer service, has to be captured, understood and carried all the way through to delivery or return. As Junior Product Manager for IT Fulfillment, you will help build and improve the services that make that happen: the order flows, data and interfaces that connect our webstore, our stores, our warehouses and our customer service teams.&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h6&gt;You will work in a small team inside the IT Fulfillment domain, alongside the Group Product Manager and our own engineers. The Group Product Manager shapes the functional direction with the business and sets priorities; together you turn it into clear requirements, well-defined tickets and working software, built with engineers and AI agents. This is a technical product role: we build our own services, so you will spend your time in data models, interfaces and requirements rather than managing a vendor’s roadmap. You start close to delivery, with support while you learn the domain, and grow into owning more of the roadmap.&lt;/h6&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Turn mapped-out functional flows into clear, buildable work: technical requirements, acceptance criteria and user stories that engineers and AI agents can pick up without coming back with questions.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the detail as both product manager and business analyst: the data model, the way systems talk to each other, and the edge cases nobody thought of yet.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Break large changes into chunks that can be built, tested and released safely, and keep the backlog in a state where work can start at any moment.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with engineers day to day in refinement, planning, reviews and releases, and use our AI tooling to draft, structure and pressure-test the work before it reaches them.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Design our order data and interfaces so that AI agents can read, reason over and act on them as reliably as our own systems do.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Create visibility across the end-to-end fulfillment journey, so anyone from a customer service agent to a supply chain lead can see where an order is and what happened to it, and turn that into measures the business trusts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Take on discovery for smaller and mid-sized roadmap items as your domain knowledge builds: the options, the trade-offs and the recommendation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Who you are&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Business analysis experience: 2+ years of hands-on experience as a Business Analyst or Product Owner. You have written functional and technical specifications, worked directly with developers, and been accountable for the detail being right. The analysis craft is what we are hiring for.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Domain experience: That experience is in fulfillment, order management, supply chain, e-commerce or retail operations. You know what an order, a shipment, an allocation and a return actually are, and what it costs operationally when one goes wrong.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Eye for detail: You chase the last open question rather than leaving it for someone else to find in production.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;AI-native mindset: You already work with tools like Claude and Cursor every day to analyse, draft, prototype and check your own thinking, and you know what to hand over and what to validate yourself.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Technical fluency: You can hold your own in a technical conversation without being an engineer, and you say “I don’t understand that yet” rather than guessing.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Communication: You are a clear writer who asks the uncomfortable question early rather than the polite one late.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Education: Bachelor’s or Master’s degree in Business, Technology, or a related field, or equivalent experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h5&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you will get&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h5&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Autonomy: We empower you to take ownership, make meaningful decisions, and drive impact close to our customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Growth: You will develop within a high-performance digital product environment, increasing your business impact and decision scope over time.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Corporate Social Responsibility: Our commitment to sustainability and ethical business is unwavering. We work exclusively with suppliers who uphold the highest standards, in alignment with the International Labour Organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Style: Immerse yourself in a world of beautifully crafted, high-quality products, and enjoy a 40% discount on Suitsupply products.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Compensation: We offer a competitive salary based on relevant skills and experience.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/suitsupply/junior-product-manager-it-fulfillment-amsterdam-209861","tags":["IT Development"],"job_types":[],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793062521},{"slug":"customer-solutions-engineer-rotterdam-93891","company_name":"Payter B.V.","title":"Customer Solutions Engineer","description":"<p><span style="color:#000000">Als ervaren Customer Solutions Engineer&nbsp; bij Payter ben jij dé expert die klanten helpt bij complexe technische vraagstukken, het diagnosticeren van problemen en het oplossen van geëscaleerde klantvragen. Je begeleidt gebruikers door geavanceerde troubleshooting van onze producten, geeft deskundig advies en verzorgt producttrainingen als het belangrijkste technische aanspreekpunt. Als diepgaande specialist van het Payter-platform deel je best-practice advies en werk je nauw samen met diverse interne teams om complexe of unieke technische escalaties succesvol op te lossen.&nbsp;</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Taken en verantwoordelijkheden</span></strong></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Onderzoeken en oplossen van complexe technische problemen, vragen over softwareversies en hardware-uitdagingen, inclusief ondersteuning bij updates, transactiefouten en de doorstroom van telemetriedata.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Verzorgen van geavanceerde terminalconfiguraties, remote diagnostics en support bij de uitrol, evenals het oplossen van netwerkproblemen (wifi, 5G, LAN) en integraties van randapparatuur.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Fungeren als dé technische autoriteit op het gebied van Payter-hardware en -software, waaronder cloud-API's, TCP/IP-socketconnectiviteit en fysieke installatieprocedures.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Bieden van deskundig technisch advies aan gebruikers over de beste oplossingen voor integratie en dagelijks gebruik.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Efficiënt beheren van supporttickets en het leveren van gedetailleerde technische oplossingen via telefoon, e-mail, video of chat.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Nauw samenwerken met collega's en engineering-teams om een klantgerichte service te leveren, kwaliteitsstandaarden te waarborgen en operationele workflows te stroomlijnen.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Nauwkeurig documenteren van alle technische interacties en het ontwikkelen van best practices voor de interne kennisbank.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Signaleren en delen van kansen voor product- en procesverbeteringen op basis van klantfeedback, om zo de algehele gebruikerservaring te blijven optimaliseren.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Over Payter</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Bij Payter zijn we pioniers en leiders op het gebied van contactloze en cashless betaaloplossingen in uiteenlopende markten, zoals elektrisch laden (EV), openbaar vervoer, retail, horeca, vending, goede doelen en parkeren. Het flexibele Payter-platform ondersteunt een breed scala aan betaaltechnologieën (waaronder NFC, EMV, Apple Pay en Google Pay), internationale bankprocessen, closed-loop betaal- en loyaliteitssystemen, en telemetrie.</span></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Door continue innovatie en in-house ontwikkeling herdefiniëren we hoe verkopers in contact staan met hun klanten. We stellen hen in staat om de omzet te verhogen, de gebruikerservaring te verbeteren en realtime toegang te krijgen tot verkoop- en prestatiedata. Onze hoogwaardige producten ondersteunen technologieën zoals Contact &amp; Contactless EMV, Mifare, WiFi, 5G, Bluetooth en touchscreens. Ze hebben een extreem lange levensduur, voldoen aan internationale standaarden, blinken uit in design, en zijn uiterst gebruiksvriendelijk en eenvoudig te integreren.</span></p> <br> <ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je hebt minimaal 2 jaar ervaring in een integratie-supportrol, of 3 tot 4 jaar in een technische supportfunctie voor diverse producten.</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je hebt praktische kennis van HTTP, JSON/XML APIs, en TCP/IP-socketcommunicatie.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je kunt goed overweg met Postman en Swagger; ervaring met softwareontwikkeling is een grote pre.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je bent bij voorkeur bekend met industrieprotocollen zoals OCPP/OCPI, MDB of EMV.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je hebt een brede achtergrond op het gebied van technische support, testen, documentatie en training.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je beschikt over bewezen probleemoplossende vaardigheden en een proactieve gedrevenheid om te leren hoe nieuwe technologieën werken.</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je bent sociaal vaardig, spreekt vloeiend professioneel Engels en hebt een oprechte klantgerichte mindset.</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je beheerst de Nederlandse taal.</span></p></li></ul><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Je bent minimaal 3 dagen per week aanwezig op kantoor.</span></p></li></ul><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Voldoe je niet aan alle eisen, maar ben je er wel van overtuigd dat je de kwaliteiten voor deze functie in huis hebt? Dan nodigen we je uit om toch te solliciteren. We laten ons graag overtuigen.</span></p><p style="min-height: 1.7em;"></p><p><strong><span style="color:#000000">Wat bieden wij?</span></strong></p><p><span style="color:#000000">Bij Payter geloven we dat een fijne werkomgeving de basis is voor succes. Daarom bieden wij jou:</span></p><ul><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een verzorgde lunch op kantoor, zodat je samen met collega's kunt genieten van een goede pauze.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">25 vakantiedagen om voldoende tijd te nemen voor ontspanning.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">12 Balance Days per jaar, iedere maand ontvang je een extra vrije dag voor een gezonde werk-privébalans.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een aantrekkelijke pensioenregeling, waarbij jij slechts 3,6% van de premie bijdraagt en Payter het grootste deel voor haar rekening neemt.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Ruimte voor groei, met volop professionele ontwikkelingsmogelijkheden en trainingen.</span></p></li><li><p><span style="color:#000000">Een goed bereikbaar kantoor in Rotterdam.</span></p></li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/payter-bv/customer-solutions-engineer-rotterdam-93891","tags":["Integration"],"job_types":["Mid","fulltime fixed term"],"location":"Rotterdam, Zuid-Holland, Nederland","created_at":1793051487},{"slug":"customer-success-associate-amsterdam-174089","company_name":"Horizon3Ai","title":"Customer Success Associate","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Get to Know Us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Horizon3.ai is a fast-growing, remote cybersecurity company dedicated to the mission of enabling organizations to proactively find and fix and verify exploitable attack vectors before criminals exploit them. Our flagship product, the NodeZeroTM platform, delivers production-safe autonomous pentests and other key assessment operations that scale across the largest internal, external, cloud, and hybrid cloud environments. NodeZero has been adopted by organizations of all sizes, from small educational institutions to government agencies and Global 100 enterprises. It is used by ITOps/SecOps teams, consulting pentesters, and MSSPs and MSPs. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are a fusion of former U.S. Special Operations cyber operators, startup engineers, and formerly frustrated cybersecurity practitioners. We're committed to helping solve our common security problems: ineffective security tools, false positives resulting in alert fatigue, blind spots, "checkbox” security culture, cybersecurity skills shortage, and the long lead time and expense of hiring outside consultants. Collectively, we are a team of learn it alls, committed to a culture of respect, collaboration, ownership, and results.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong> What you will do: </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Customer Success Associate in EMEA, you will play a key role in scaling and strengthening our international post-sales experience as part of a growing global Customer Success organization. You will serve as a strategic advisor to a portfolio of mid-market customers, partnering directly with technical and business stakeholders to drive adoption, value realization, retention, and growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You’ll collaborate cross-functionally with Sales, Product, Engineering, and Support while helping shape and evolve the Customer Success experience across the EMEA region.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>We are open to candidates based in the Netherlands who are willing to work in a hybrid model, at least 1 day per week in our Amsterdam office.</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage a portfolio of EMEA mid-market customers as their primary post-sales technical advisor, developing a deep understanding of the NodeZero platform to guide successful adoption</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cultivate champions with security leaders—from analysts to CISOs—and guide them through the lifecycle of adoption, expansion, and advocacy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deliver technical onboarding and enablement to drive adoption of NodeZero, including advanced features like Tripwires, Insights, and Rapid Response, ensuring customers realize maximum value</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proactively identify customer needs and potential challenges, suggesting solutions that improve their experience and enhance their cybersecurity posture</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner closely with IT and Security teams (SOC, red/blue teams, AppSec, etc.) to help interpret pentest results, prioritize remediation, and guide long-term offensive security strategy</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Collaborate closely with Sales and Renewals teams to drive retention and growth by identifying expansion opportunities, aligning on account strategy, and ensuring a seamless renewal process</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a customer advocate, relaying customer feedback and technical issues to our internal teams to help drive the evolution of our product and services</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Conduct regular check-ins and quarterly business reviews to align on strategy, secure executive buy-in, and showcase business outcomes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to documentation, training materials, and repeatable playbooks to scale technical success across the region</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain detailed records of customer health and touchpoints using internal CS platforms</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">3+ years in Customer Success, Technical Account Management, Client Services, within a SaaS cybersecurity environment</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">In-depth knowledge of cybersecurity practices and principles</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep understanding of enterprise security, information technology, cloud, or offensive security is highly preferred</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong customer acumen—able to align solutions to business priorities and present clearly to both technical and executive stakeholders</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience managing a book of business with revenue targets (ARR, NRR, GRR)</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup or high-growth company experience is preferred; you thrive in fast-paced, ambiguous environments</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Location: based in the Netherlands and able to work in a hybrid model, at least 1 day per week in our Amsterdam office</strong></p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Comfortable with tools like Salesforce, Gainsight, and JIRA; detail-oriented and organized</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">English fluency required; fluency in French, Spanish, or German preferred</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"> </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Perks of Horizon3.ai</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Inclusive Team: We value diversity and promote an inclusive culture where everyone can thrive.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Growth Opportunities: Be part of a dynamic and growing team with numerous career development opportunities.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Innovative Culture: Work in a collaborative environment that encourages creativity and out-of-the-box thinking.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Compensation: We offer competitive salary, equity and benefits. Our benefits include health, vision &amp; dental insurance for you and your family, a flexible vacation policy, and generous parental leave.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Compensation and Values</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Horizon3, we believe that our people are our greatest asset, and our compensation philosophy reflects this core value. We are committed to fostering an environment where all employees feel valued, respected, and rewarded for their contributions. Our compensation structure is designed to be fair, competitive, and transparent, ensuring that every team member is recognized and compensated equitably across roles, levels, and locations.</p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Depending on experience, the compensation range for this position is: €70,000 - €85,000 OTE 80/20 split annually. The exact salary will be determined based on the selected candidate’s location, qualifications, experience, and relevant skills.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Additional compensation: All full-time roles are eligible for an equity package in the form of stock options.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>You Belong Here</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Horizon3 is not just an equal opportunity employer - we are a community that values diversity, equity, and inclusion as fundamental principles of our culture and success. We are dedicated to fostering a workplace where everyone feels welcome and respected, regardless of race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, genetic information, marital status, hair length or any other legally protected status by law.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Our commitment to diversity and inclusion means we strive to attract, develop, and retain a workforce that reflects the varied communities we serve. We believe that diverse perspectives drive innovation and strengthen our ability to create cutting-edge cybersecurity solutions. At Horizon3, every team member is valued and supported in an environment that encourages personal and professional growth.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We welcome candidates from all backgrounds and experiences, and we encourage all qualified individuals to apply. Come be a part of Horizon3, where your unique contributions are recognized, and your potential is limitless.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Other Duties</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Please note this job description is not designed to cover or contain a comprehensive listing of activities, duties or responsibilities that are required of the employee. Duties, responsibilities, and activities may change at any time with or without notice. </p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Application Note</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">In any materials you submit, you may redact or remove age-identifying information such as age, date of birth, or dates of school attendance or graduation. You will not be penalized for redacting or removing this information.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/horizon3ai/customer-success-associate-amsterdam-174089","tags":["Customer"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam, Netherlands","created_at":1793050818},{"slug":"biztalk-and-azure-integration-developer-eindhoven-378254","company_name":"Kryptos Technologies limited","title":"Biztalk and Azure integration Developer","description":"<h2><strong>Job Title: BizTalk & Azure Team Lead Consultant</strong></h2><p><strong>Location:</strong> Eindhoven, Netherlands – 3 days onsite per week<br><strong>Contract:</strong> 6 months initially, with possible extension<br><strong>Engagement:</strong> Contract</p><p><strong>Role Overview</strong></p><p>We are looking for an experienced <strong>BizTalk & Azure Team Lead Consultant</strong> to join an enterprise integration team in Eindhoven. The role will focus on designing, developing, supporting and modernising integration solutions using <strong>Microsoft BizTalk Server and Azure Integration Services</strong>.</p><p>The ideal candidate will have strong hands-on BizTalk experience, combined with solid Azure integration expertise and the ability to lead technical delivery within an enterprise environment.</p>