li><li><p>REST APIs</p></li><li><p>Visual Studio</p></li></ul><ul><li><p>Strong understanding of <strong>messaging, SOA and integration patterns</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Experience with <strong>Azure Integration Services</strong>, particularly Logic Apps, Functions, Service Bus, API Management, Storage and Key Vault.</p></li><li><p>Experience with <strong>Azure DevOps and/or TFS</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Experience implementing <strong>CI/CD pipelines and automated deployments</strong>.</p></li><li><p>Experience supporting production integration environments and resolving complex technical issues.</p></li><li><p>Experience with <strong>cloud migration and application modernisation</strong> projects.</p></li><li><p>Familiarity with <strong>Agile/Scrum</strong> methodologies.</p></li><li><p><strong>Microsoft Azure certification(s)</strong> would be highly desirable.</p></li></ul><p><strong>Key Skills</strong></p><p><strong>BizTalk Server | Azure Integration Services | C# | .NET | Azure Logic Apps | Azure Functions | Azure Service Bus | Azure API Management | Azure DevOps | TFS | XML | XSD | XPath | XSLT | SOAP | REST | CI/CD | Enterprise Integration | Cloud Migration | Application Modernisation</strong></p><p></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/kryptos-technologies-limited/biztalk-and-azure-integration-developer-eindhoven-378254","tags":["Software Development"],"job_types":["Self-employed/freelance (zzp - zelfstandige zonder personeel)","freelance","professional / experienced"],"location":"Eindhoven","created_at":1793050237},{"slug":"senior-engineering-manager-amsterdam-185168","company_name":"Mollie","title":"Senior Engineering Manager","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your opportunity:</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Since 2004, we've had one clear goal: to make payments and money management effortless for every business in Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, more than 250,000 companies use Mollie to get paid, manage money and grow, with products designed to be simple, scalable, and dependable.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">With 950+ Mollies across 14+ locations, we care deeply about autonomy and craft. So we work in small teams, with real ownership, and we trust you to make the right decisions.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're building for the long term, so we provide the tools you need, processes you can rely on, and a balanced work environment to help you do work you're proud of.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Sound like your kind of place? Let's build together.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a <strong>Senior Engineering Manager</strong>, you'll lead the technical roadmap and delivery of our existing and new products. You’ll collaborate with cross-functional teams to shape strategy and product direction, while also representing the team in technical discussions with key partners. In this fast-paced environment, your impact will be highly visible, driving customer experience improvements and contributing to the company’s success.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead a growing engineering team of 20+ engineers, with a hands-on leadership approach expected from all engineering managers</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bring strong technical expertise and a proven track record in large-scale distributed systems and/or guiding teams through complex technical transitions</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive strategic technical decisions in collaboration with cross-functional teams, and lead cross-domain technical initiatives that align with overall business and product goals</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Identify improvements within the team, propose actionable solutions, and coordinate efforts to improve team velocity and effectiveness</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Help shape the broader domain vision, influence strategic direction, and set goals for ongoing product improvement</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Balance hands-on engineering with big picture thinking, taking pride in mentoring and developing high performing teams</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Maintain a results driven mindset focused on delivering impact at scale and speed</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you have:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Strong leadership and team development skills</strong>: You set clear goals, provide transparent feedback, mentor engineers, and support career growth while driving high-impact results.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Proven management experience</strong>: With 5+ years in a leadership role, you’ve demonstrated success in hiring, retaining, and developing top engineering talent.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Commitment to engineering excellence</strong>: Bring hands-on experience building scalable, resilient, and full stack systems in diverse environments, leading by example and setting a high bar .</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Bias for action</strong>: You believe in moving fast without compromising quality. You’re not afraid to make mistakes as long as they’re opportunities to learn and improve.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Mentorship and teaching mindset</strong>: Invest in the growth of others through code reviews, architectural guidance, or coaching, you help engineers refine their skills, build confidence, and take on new challenges.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Collaborative spirit</strong>: You foster a culture of openness and trust, you value feedback, encourage peer learning, and support team-wide development.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Always Be Shipping Mindset:</strong> It’s about consistently delivering value to customers, where speed and quality go hand in hand.</p></li></ul><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Please apply with your CV in English</strong></em></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><em><strong>Kindly note that visa and relocation support is not offered for this particular role.</strong></em></p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mollie/senior-engineering-manager-amsterdam-185168","tags":["Engineering"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793040014},{"slug":"head-of-product-cards-amsterdam-477101","company_name":"Mollie","title":"Head of Product - Cards","description":"<p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Head of Product - Cards - Amsterdam </strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build with us</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Businesses deserve better from finance. Less friction, more freedom. Since 2004, Mollie has been on a mission to make payments and money management effortless for every business in Europe.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Today, more than 250,000 companies trust our all-in-one platform to get paid, manage money and grow on their terms. Simple, scalable and built with real businesses in mind.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're one of Europe's fastest-growing fintechs, with 950+ Mollies across 14+ locations. Our people make this growth possible. We move fast, build with purpose and care deeply about our customers. Whether you're solving problems, building market-leading products or exploring how AI can make work smarter, you'll have the freedom to create and the trust to deliver.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're ready to grow, shape the future of fintech and join an ambitious, high-performing team, this is the place for you.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Your impact</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cards is one of the most strategically important products at Mollie. It is the primary payment method operating at a global scale and the central enabler for Mollie to serve larger, more sophisticated merchants. As the accountable lead for online cards acceptance, you will own one of the highest net revenue-generating areas in the business, and your work will directly shape Mollie's ability to compete for and retain enterprise and mid-market merchants.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As the Head of Product for Cards Acquiring, you will own the end-to-end product strategy and execution for one of the most critical payment methods. You will bridge the gap between heavy technical infrastructure and high-impact commercial enablement. Leading a cross-functional team of around 20 people that includes product delivery managers, a product partnership person, a dedicated data person, and a PMM, you will scale Mollie’s cards capabilities beyond Europe, unlock new merchant categories, and ensure our proposition wins the hearts of highly sophisticated merchants. You will also work directly with payment schemes and external partners, making decisions that influence both the product roadmap and Mollie's broader positioning in the market.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The cards domain is expected to become an increasingly primary driver of Mollie's growth over time, with the potential for the online and in-person card acceptance platforms to converge and expand the scope of this role significantly. If you want to own something that matters at a company that is moving fast in the right direction, this is it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you'll ship</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">End-to-end product ownership: own the full cards acceptance product lifecycle—from deep technical infrastructure and processing stability to commercial enablement.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Go-To-Market &amp; commercial enablement: lead the GTM strategy for new card features in tight lockstep with Product Marketing (PMM) and Commercial teams. You'll translate complex technical capabilities into crystal-clear value propositions that our sales teams can run with.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Global scale: drive the geographic expansion of our cards product, building out capabilities beyond Europe to support Mollie’s international growth.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Portfolio optimisation: Identify untapped merchant vertical opportunities and make data-driven decisions to maximise net revenue across the entire cards portfolio.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team Leadership: Manage, coach, and scale a high-performing product team.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What You’ll Bring</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Commercial &amp; GTM Strategy: A proven track record of launching successful financial/payment products. You know how to price, position, and package features alongside PMM to win market share.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partnership acumen: deep understanding of direct vs. indirect relationship strategies in the payments ecosystem and their respective commercial implications.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Technical depth: you aren't afraid of complexity. You can comfortably navigate the underlying technical architecture of cards acquiring, including the intricacies of the PCI compliance landscape.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Operational scale: experience managing operations-heavy environments and a proven ability to build scalable organisational structures that handle massive transaction volumes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Customer obsession: this is non-negotiable at Mollie. You have a relentless drive to understand merchant pain points and build products that genuinely delight them.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Leadership: experience leading and developing cross-functional teams. You know how to cultivate a culture of high performance, accountability, and psychological safety.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow your way</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Mollie, growth is personal. We believe everyone should have the chance to develop their skills, explore new challenges and shape their career on their own terms.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll get regular feedback and performance reviews to support your development, with fair and transparent salary reviews along the way. Many Mollies move into new roles or take on new projects to stretch themselves, and we actively hire from within to help you take the next step.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">No matter if you're aiming for promotion, exploring a different career path or building new skills, you'll be supported with the tools, trust and opportunities to grow your way.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Unlock your full potential and join us to eliminate financial bureaucracy</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">If you're excited by the idea of building what's next, for yourself and for thousands of businesses across Europe, we'd love to hear from you. Apply with your CV (in English) using the form below.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Want a peek behind the scenes? Check out what life at Mollie is really like.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>AI at Mollie</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We believe in Always Be Shipping, and AI brings that philosophy to life across every team, every role, every day.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">AI is core to how we build. It helps us move faster, simplify work and make smarter decisions, creating real impact for the businesses we serve. We're looking for people who are excited to use AI to shape the future of finance with us.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><br /></p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/mollie/head-of-product-cards-amsterdam-477101","tags":["Product and Delivery"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793040014},{"slug":"business-development-manager-amsterdam-56154","company_name":"ATMET","title":"Business Development Manager / Accountmanager Buitendienst – Logistics & Packaging","description":"<h2>About AtMet Group</h2><p>Since 1995, AtMet Group has manufactured cargo securing solutions that keep goods safe at sea, on the road and on rail. Our core products are dunnage airbags, inflatable bags that fill voids between cargo to prevent movement, and lashing systems, straps and securing equipment for containers and other transport units.</p><p>We manufacture in China and the USA, operate a French office (opened in 2021), and hold local stock in France and Rotterdam. The Netherlands and Belgium are our next step, and you will lead it.</p><h2>The Role</h2><p>You will be our first commercial presence in the Benelux, with real ownership of the market. You will:</p><ul><li>Win new B2B customers in the Netherlands and Belgium, starting with the Rotterdam port area</li><li>Recruit and develop distributors of cargo securing products</li><li>Prospect logistics companies, freight forwarders, exporters, manufacturers and packaging distributors</li><li>Visit customers, present our range and run product demonstrations</li><li>Spot high-volume opportunities and new market segments</li><li>Keep your CRM pipeline up to date and report regularly on activity and results</li><li>Represent AtMet at relevant trade shows and industry events</li></ul><h2>Your Profile</h2><h3>Essential</h3><ul><li>3+ years of B2B sales experience with a track record of winning new customers (logistics, transport, packaging or a related sector is a plus)</li><li>Fluent Dutch and English, written and spoken</li><li>Autonomous, self-organized and comfortable with field prospecting</li><li>Strong communication and negotiation skills</li><li>Experience with a CRM and Microsoft Office</li><li>Category B driving licence</li></ul><h3>Nice to have</h3><ul><li>Existing network in the Rotterdam port, freight forwarding or industrial packaging community</li><li>Knowledge of cargo securing or intermodal transport</li></ul><h2>What We Offer</h2><ul><li>Autonomy: you manage your own schedule and customer visits, against clearly agreed targets</li><li>A market to build: the Benelux is open territory, with local stock already in Rotterdam to support fast delivery to your customers</li><li>Fixed salary + commission: €4,500–€5,500 gross/month, plus commission on the new business you win</li><li>Room to grow: more responsibility as the business expands</li><li>Local employment: employed under Dutch employment law through an Employer of Record</li><li>Everything you need: laptop, phone</li><li>Travel covered: mileage allowance for your own vehicle, short-term car rental when needed</li><li>Home-based: with regular customer visits</li></ul><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":true,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/atmet/business-development-manager-amsterdam-56154","tags":["Remote","Business Development"],"job_types":["Payroll employment (payrolling)","professional / experienced"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793046749},{"slug":"events-community-manager-amsterdam-4220","company_name":"Tebi","title":"Events & Community Manager","description":"<h2><strong>About us:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Tebi is creating the first Connected Restaurant Management System that makes hospitality flow. In one seamless platform, Tebi embeds sales, reservations, kitchen prep, payments, and all the data that powers it, creating smooth service and intuitive insights.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">Founded by Arnout Schuijff, co-founder of Adyen, and backed by €50 million in funding from Index Ventures &amp; CapitalG, Tebi is built in service of hospitality first. Thousands of restaurants, cafés, bars, and coffee shops across the Netherlands, UK, Italy, Spain, Germany, Denmark and Finland already love running on Tebi.</p><h2><strong>About the role:</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurant owners trust other restaurant owners. They listen to the chef down the street, their wine supplier and their accountant long before they listen to an ad. That's why our events work. When we launched in Berlin, we hosted a four-hands dinner with two local merchants and a well-known food creator. We believe that’s what builds credibility, trust, and ultimately a warm prospect list.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re hiring an Events &amp; Community Manager to turn that into a program that runs in several markets at the same time. You’ll plan and run our partner and owned events, and find new ways to grow Tebi through the hospitality community in each city, neighbourhood and market. You’ll work closely with our local sales teams so every event and partnership turns into real conversations.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a hands-on role. One week you'll be hosting a merchant dinner in Milan, the next you'll be setting up a distributor breakfast in Amsterdam. You'll report to the Head of Marketing and work closely with our Marketing team to extend these programs to our channel ecosystem, plus align closely with the General Managers and Account Managers in each market.</p><h2><strong>What you'll be doing:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Run events across markets:</strong> Plan and deliver partner and owned events in 2–3 markets at a time, from intimate merchant dinners and industry breakfasts to city launches. You own the calendar, budget, venues, suppliers, guest lists and the plan for the night.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build the playbook as you go:</strong> Turn each event into templates, checklists and supplier lists, so we can launch a city campaign in weeks, not months. Improve them after every event.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Build local partner networks:</strong> Find the people operators already trust: drinks distributors, wholesalers, food creators, hospitality associations, accountants and the advisers who help new venues open. Build partnerships that bring us introductions and referrals, not just logos.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Put our merchants front and center:</strong> Work with our best merchants as hosts and anchors, so prospects hear about Tebi from the people they respect.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Turn connections into pipeline:</strong> Agree with local Sales and Account Management who to involve, how to follow up and who owns what conversations. Track every event in HubSpot from invite to demo to signed merchant.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Grow Tebi through the community:</strong> Find new ways to reach operators through the people and places they already trust, in each city, neighborhood and across borders. Keep guests and partners engaged after events, so one introduction leads to the next.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Open new community channels:</strong> Test new ways to grow through our close-knit industry, such as an affiliate or referral program for partners, sharing useful insights from our merchants, and showing up in the forums and groups where operators talk shop.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Capture the stories:</strong> Work with our creative team and relevant freelancers to turn events and partner moments into social content, case studies and sales material.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>How we'll measure success:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Events delivered each quarter across markets, on time and on budget</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Demos, pipeline and new merchants from each event and partnership</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Introductions, referrals and leads from partners, affiliates and community channels</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Cost per demo compared with our other channels</p></li></ul><h2><strong>What you’ll bring:</strong></h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Have built something people show up for: an event series, a supper club, a community, a program. You can point to what it led to, not just how many people came</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Feel at home in hospitality. You've worked in or around restaurants, bars or food and drink brands, and you're comfortable leading a room full of operators</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Are high agency. You own your calendar, your relationships and your results, and you don't wait to be told what to do</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Build your own playbook when there isn't one, and you enjoy doing the work as much as planning it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Know the difference between a real community and a guest list</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">See growth opportunities beyond events, and are curious enough to test them</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Can run several markets at once without dropping details, and are happy to travel regularly</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track what you do: comfortable with a CRM (HubSpot a plus), UTMs and simple reporting</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Speak fluent English. Dutch, German, Italian, Spanish or a Nordic language is a plus</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em">Typically this means 3–5 years in events, community, field marketing or partnerships, but we care more about what you've built than how long you've been doing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>This role isn't for you if:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'd rather plan the program than run it</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You need a fixed playbook and a clear org chart to get going</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">You're not willing to roll up your sleeves on the night</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Benefits:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Start-up Equity</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive Salary</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lunch Provided in Office</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Team building events</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Unlimited time off</p></li></ul><h3><strong>What is Restaurant Software?</strong></h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">Restaurants and other merchants use various software systems such as Point of Sale (POS), Reservations, Kitchen Display Systems (KDS), Payments, Inventory, Staffing, and the list goes on. These systems all need to speak to each other which they frequently don’t. It’s a mess, and we are fixing it.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">From buying a croissant at a cafe to having dinner with friends, it’s a €4 Trillion+ global market and a critical part of everyday life in today's economy.</p><h3>How we use AI at Tebi</h3><p style="min-height:1.5em">We use AI the way our merchants use Tebi, to cut out the friction and get to what matters faster. We believe in a world where AI increases quality, efficiency and speed.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Tebi, AI isn't a policy or a checkbox, it's just part of how we work. It helps us write, analyse, build, and improve but doesn’t make the last call. If there's a smarter way to do something, we want to find it.</p><p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/tebi/events-community-manager-amsterdam-4220","tags":["Marketing"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"Amsterdam","created_at":1793029215},{"slug":"staff-product-manager-managed-detection-and-incident-response-the-hague-399868","company_name":"Eye Security","title":"Staff Product Manager – Managed Detection and Incident Response (m/f/x)","description":"<h2>About Eye Security</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Eye Security is providing cybersecurity with embedded cyber insurance solutions for organizations in Europe. Headquartered in the Netherlands, we are already over 190 FTEs and continue to grow internationally having secured our Series C funding of €60 Million!</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We combine cutting-edge technology with hands-on expertise to detect, respond to, and recover from cyber threats in real time. Our team brings together talent from intelligence, military, tech, and consulting backgrounds — all united by a shared mission: to make enterprise-grade cybersecurity accessible to every business, not just the big players.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">At Eye, you'll work on projects with an international footprint, solving real-world challenges and helping to build a safer digital future for our clients.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>About this role</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">As our client base continues to grow rapidly across Europe, this role will play a key strategic part in scaling our Managed Detection and Response (MDR), Endpoint Detection and Response (EDR), and Incident Response (IR) capabilities.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">You'll take full ownership of the product strategy and roadmap for this space. Collaborating with our engineers, product designers, security operations, product marketing, and cross-functional leadership, you will ensure that our platform evolves with our customers' needs and delivers maximum impact at scale.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This is a senior individual contributor and thought leadership role designed for someone who thrives on autonomy, discovery, and leading cross-functional product development in a fast-growing environment. You'll be the strategic voice shaping our product direction, mentoring product managers, and influencing broader company strategy.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p><h2>What you will do</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Own and communicate the long-term product vision and strategy for MDR, EDR, and IR. Define strategic priorities, influence company OKRs, and drive cross-functional alignment around product direction.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Define and own the product roadmap for MDR, EDR, and IR, ensuring alignment with company vision, market opportunity, and customer needs. </p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Drive discovery practices to deeply understand customer needs, problems, and pain points.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Lead and mentor product managers and junior team members. Work closely with Engineering, Product Design, Security Operations, Product Marketing, Customer Success, and Sales to deliver successful outcomes and build high-performing teams.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with Product Marketing to define comprehensive go-to-market strategies, product launches, and market positioning that drive competitive advantage.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Manage external relationships and partnerships, especially with EDR vendors and MDR technology providers, ensuring alignment with our MSP and partner strategy.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Stay at the forefront of cybersecurity trends, emerging technologies, and industry best practices.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Contribute to the evolution of our internal processes, tooling, and product culture. Champion agile methodologies, data-driven execution, and continuous experimentation.</p></li></ul><h2>What you will need</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">7+ years of Product Management experience, with at least 4 years in senior or staff-level roles owning end-to-end delivery of software products in B2B SaaS or similar environments.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Deep cybersecurity domain expertise.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of successfully delivering complex software products in fast-paced environments using product discovery, data-driven decision making, and agile methodologies.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong business acumen: understanding of go-to-market strategy, sales enablement, and how product drives revenue and customer success.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Excellent communication and stakeholder management skills, with the ability to present complex strategies clearly to technical, commercial, and executive audiences.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Strong analytical and problem-solving mindset, with comfort in ambiguity and the ability to make sound decisions with incomplete information.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Fluent English</p></li></ul><h2>Nice-to-have</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Startup or scale-up background at a high-growth company.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience building or scaling product management teams and processes.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exposure to OKR-driven product development and metrics-focused product management.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Experience working with MSP or partner-led go-to-market models.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Track record of navigating successful product pivots or strategic repositioning.</p></li></ul><h2>What we offer</h2><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A meaningful mission: protect organizations across Europe from real-world cyber threats.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with top-tier professionals from national CERTs, intelligence agencies, and leading tech backgrounds.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Full strategic ownership of a mission-critical product area in a high-growth cybersecurity scale-up.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Mentorship and growth: lead and develop the next generation of product managers; grow into broader strategy and leadership roles.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Weekly lunches (NL) and Thursday socials to stay connected.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">A generous time-off policy, including wellbeing and volunteering days.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Competitive salary and benefits package, including equity participation.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em"></p></li></ul><h2>Are you up for it?</h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">We look forward to receiving your application.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We are an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to making our hiring process accessible to everyone. If you need a reasonable accommodation to apply or interview for this role, please inform the TA team.</p><p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl">Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>","remote":false,"url":"https://www.arbeitnow.nl/jobs/companies/eye-security/staff-product-manager-managed-detection-and-incident-response-the-hague-399868","tags":["Technology"],"job_types":["Full Time"],"location":"The Hague - hybrid","created_at":1793029214},{"slug":"staff-solutions-engineer-embedded-finance-amsterdam-158753","company_name":"Airwallex","title":"Staff Solutions Engineer - Embedded Finance","description":"<h2><strong>About Airwallex</strong></h2><p style="min-height:1.5em">Airwallex is the AI-native financial operating system for a real-time, intelligent economy. More than 675,000 businesses, including McLaren Racing, Qantas, SHEIN, and TikTok, use us, directly or through our platform partners, to run their financial operations or build and monetize financial products of their own.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We started in Melbourne in 2015 to build the infrastructure global commerce runs on. We're the regulated backbone behind global payments: not by accident, but by design. A decade plus, 85+ licenses, and a financial infrastructure spanning North America, Europe, the Middle East, and Asia-Pacific.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We're co-headquartered in San Francisco and Singapore, with more than 2,700 people across 27 offices. We hire builders with founder-level energy, people who move fast with good judgment, dig in with real curiosity, and make calls from first principles rather than waiting to be told what to do. Read our<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer nofollow" href="https://www.airwallex.com/en-us/operating-principles"> <u>operating principles</u></a> to see it in full.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>About the team</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">The Merchant Services team partners with our clients to realise their full potential through the adoption of Airwallex products that drive their growth and success. We influence revenue growth across our entire product portfolio and collaborate with sales, strategy, product, and engineering teams to provide the best experience for our most valued customers. Our team works alongside commercial teams throughout the pre-sales, solution design, and API integration stages, serving as the single technical point of contact and trusted advisor for our clients. We are committed to empowering businesses with the tools our clients need to succeed in a dynamic market</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>What you’ll do</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">As a Staff Solutions Engineer you will <strong>own the technical pre-sales and implementation of AirWallex solutions for complex client engagements </strong>that bring our global payments and financial products to life for enterprise partners, shopping carts, and payment gateways. You will turn agreed business requirements into solution designs and actionable plans, orchestrating cross-functional teams and external stakeholders to deliver on time, on scope, and to a high quality bar. You’ll provide technical trust, ensuring that every phase from pre‑sales through go‑live and early optimisation runs smoothly.</p><p style="min-height:1.5em">This role is based in Amsterdam<strong> (3 days in office)</strong>, with implementation coverage across EMEA.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Responsibilities:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Act as a trusted technical advisor to customers and internal teams on high-value implementations and expansions, shaping integration approaches, system configuration, and overall solution design.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Partner with implementation and account management teams to translate customer requirements into scalable architectures.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work with sales teams on technical discovery to understand customer systems, data flows, and workflows, and recommend a best-fit integration blueprint, including when and how to leverage APIs and third-party connectors.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Work hands-on with customers to troubleshoot integration hurdles and guide them through complex configuration decisions, focusing on designing robust, maintainable implementations rather than writing code directly.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Create and maintain internal documentation, playbooks, and lightweight tooling that make it easier for the wider team to support integration-heavy use cases at scale.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Channel customer pain points and integration feedback into Product and Engineering, influencing the roadmap and prioritisation of features that materially improve implementation outcomes.</p></li></ul><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Who you are</strong></p><p style="min-height:1.5em">We’re looking for people who meet the minimum requirements for this role. The preferred qualifications are great to have, but are not mandatory.</p><div style="min-height:1.2em;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:0px"> </div><p style="min-height:1.5em"><strong>Minimum qualifications:</strong></p><ul style="min-height:1.5em"><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Bachelor’s degree in a related field (e.g. Business, Finance, Engineering, Information Systems) or equivalent practical experience.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years of experience in <strong>technical pre-sales</strong>, managing complex, multi‑stakeholder technology or financial services implementations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">8+ years of <strong>client‑facing delivery or professional services</strong> experience in a high‑paced environment (e.g. SaaS, fintech, consulting, systems integration, enterprise implementation).</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Proven track record of successfully delivering cross‑functional projects with stakeholders from diverse backgrounds and job functions, including C‑level executives, technical teams, and operations.</p></li><li><p style="min-height:1.5em">Exceptional written and verbal communication and presentation skills, including the ability to lead steering meetings, write clear status updates, and influence decisions wi